{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition","id":1531964,"title":"Your hypothetical Mage 30th edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-04T11:40:05-08:00","id":1531964,"title":"Your hypothetical Mage 30th edition","content":"So I didn't see anything mentioning it in any of the other threads, but Mage is 30 years old now as of August last year, so huzzah! confetti poppers, etc.<br /> <br /> Considering 20th Anniversary edition is itself almost 10 years old now, I started wondering what people thought needed updated in the settings for the past decade?<br /> <br /> Note: This is not a Mage 5th edition thread. Based on other 5th edition books if and when that happens it will be more of a soft reboot. Also lets not bring frustrations over 5th edition here. I more interested in the communities hypothetical 30th anniversary edition so to speak.<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, one thing I'd change is the Mercurial Elite, and well... just drop it all together. Onyx Path has had nearly ten years to flesh the concept out/differentiate them from Hermetic Technomagic Houses, and the best The Guide to the Traditions could do was basically &quot;Hermitic techno wizards demand the true names of tech spirits, where the Mercurial Elite respectfully brute force guess it.&quot; There is plenty that can be done to expand on the Virtual Adepts concept without leaning on mysticism as a crutch, the old vs new guard can easily be re envisioned has a &quot;hardware power vs programming skills&quot; dynamic, and between VR/AR's resurgence in public consciousness, as well as virtual currencies and AI, the name Virtual Adept seems far from dated anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T12:32:26-08:00","id":1531973,"title":"","content":"20th Anniversary editions were, for the most part, compilations of the previous editions, which lead to massive tomes that tried to fit everything into one book. For a 30th Anniversary Edition, I'd prefer something that <i>doesn't </i>try to fit everything in one book: plan to do a series of supplements to flesh out what the core book can't handle, and swim for the core book to be comparable to the size of M2 or MRev. <br /> <br /> That means two things: first, whoever writes the thing needs to be very tight on their writing; you're going to need to pack as much content into as little word count as possible. Second: even with that, you're going to need to be very selective about what you include. You <i>will not </i>be able to cover everything that M20 covers, not in the core book. <br /> <br /> Reorganize the book so that Focus goes front and center in character creation, having it be crafted in Step One, before you even get to the point of choosing which faction (if any) your mage belongs to. In my ideal book, I'd want something like <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/446015\" target=\"_blank\">Prism of Focus</a> to be integrated into the Magick system, and have that be on the <i>front end</i> of the Magick system, not tacked into the back like an afterthought. When you get to the Spheres, I'd want some hardcore rule mechanics on the development staff to go through the system with a fine-tooth comb and turn it into something not unlike what the Magick system in <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> is like. <br /> <br /> I would prioritize these sorts of things, to the point that if there's not enough room, I'd rather cut things like the Traditions et al in order to make room for a proper Magick system. <br /> <br /> More thoughts later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T13:30:10-08:00","id":1531975,"title":"","content":"Personally at the very least I'd want to mantain the base elevator pitch of the game, so have the Traditions fleshed out as the standard player faction, and describing the Technocracy as rivals/frenemies, and maybe include Tradition adjacent crafts like Ahl i Batin, Solificati, and Hollow Ones. More details write ups of the Technocracy and Disparates though could honestly wait for their own supplements if we need room for all the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","user":"Becksworth","date":". 03-04-2024, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T14:20:58-08:00","id":1531977,"title":"","content":"I would want, first and foremost, a streamlined and consistent spheres system, with the spheres having similar and easily understandable progressions and purviews. If spheres can't have the same progression then similar spheres should have similar progressions. There should be generalized rules that cover commonly occurring permutations like locking effects and setting conditions, that are easy to understand and give an indication of how to approach more niche situations. It should be clear that the game rules are game rules, not in universe metaphysics. If the magic system is done right, it shouldn't need to take up so much of the book.<br /> <br /> After that, I'd focus on fleshing out the character of the setting. The various places (the Digital Web, High Umbra, etc) should be described as characters in their own right, with a focus on how they feel and why they are important. Breathe life into the world and make it a place the characters want to visit. That also includes the Ascension War itself. It's not a place, but it heavily impacts places and I'd like to see more focus on the fallout and strangeness it unleashes.<br /> <br /> I also think its time to go back to the drawing board on the Traditions. I don't mean throw them out entirely, but many of them have origins that are incompatible with the groups they represent, usually because those origins are based on modern occult groups rather than real historical groups (or believable fictional ones). Remove those odd origins and let the Traditions be more like who they are meant to represent. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T14:28:46-08:00","id":1531979,"title":"","content":"In the pre-M20 editions, your choice of Tradition largely determined how you're Magick looks, such that if you wanted to play a witch, you did it by making a Verbena. M20 took what had previously been the Theory and Practice sections of the Tradition write-ups and made them stand-alone choices of Paradigms and Practices under the new Focus section; so now, if you want to play a witch, you make a mage with the Practice of Witchcraft. If your mage isn't engaging in Council politics, there's no longer any need for her to be a Verbena. <br /> <br /> In M30, I'd love to take that further: instead of each Tradition getting a two-page write-up and a position in the book that suggests that you pretty much have to choose a Tradition, I'd give each Paradigm and Practice a half-page spread (again, like Prism of Focus), and I'd reduce the Traditions, Conventions, and Crafts to two paragraph sketches, one of which would be akin to the Focus paragraph for the faction that's found in M20. Put more detailed write-ups for <i>all</i> of them in supplements: an M30 Guide to the Traditions, an M30 Guide to the Technocracy, and an M30 Guide to the Disparates. But you shouldn't need <i>any</i> of them to play the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T14:53:47-08:00","id":1531981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1531973#post1531973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my ideal book, I'd want something like <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/446015\" target=\"_blank\">Prism of Focus</a> to be integrated into the Magick system, and have that be on the <i>front end</i> of the Magick system, not tacked into the back like an afterthought.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've spent the last week reading <i>Prism</i> over breakfast, and I agree, it's very good. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd give each Paradigm and Practice a half-page spread (again, like Prism of Focus), and I'd reduce the Traditions, Conventions, and Crafts to two paragraph sketches </div> </div> </div>I agree. The way <i>Prism</i> treats Practices reminds me of how the 1e core described the Traditions, less organisations (though, those are certainly there), and more styles of doing magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T21:41:00-08:00","id":1531993,"title":"","content":"Oh, one thing I would have liked to gave seen was some new modern day crafts or sub tradition group. Perhaps you could flesh out the Emissaries of the Sphinx as the new prospective 10th tradition and give them some inventive new sub groups and practices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:53:37-08:00","id":1532020,"title":"","content":"What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> said.<br /> <br /> To add to that &quot;streamlined and consistent spheres system&quot;, there are several &quot;sub-systems&quot; that also could use that treatment. Wonders could use to be more streamlined and consistent.<br /> <br /> As they are now, examples are often inconsistent with how the creation system works. Wonder creation rules, and the Background costs associated, can be very obscure even in those times they're consistent, being hard to understand even for those of us that read the book several times. To say the least. I was able to understand some things thanks to these Forums after discussing what I had read several times. And even then I have many doubts.<br /> <br /> Altrough much less obscure, Countermagick it's also odd. It's not clear to me if it's an application of Spheres like any other (that would require Focus and such), or if it's an inherent power of Mages. It doesn't follow the general rules (it can't be deduced from the Sphere system that a lvl 1 on a Sphere would &quot;impede&quot; another mage's effect, and the difficulty isn't consistent). Because of that it's not transparent to me that one can extrapolate or permutate to use with other aspects of the system (Can I lower it's Diff with Quint? - I guess not) .<br /> <br /> Perhaps more than &quot;streamlined&quot; the word that I would want to use it's &quot;clear&quot;. Altrough that would likely require the former.<br /> <br /> No more &quot;hidden rules&quot; that need to be deduced from Rotes, or some particular sub-system, because the authors seem to assume them (since they're found repeatedly) but can't be deduced from the general system. Let the particular be deductible from the general every time that would be possible, and when it isn't let's be clear that this is a particularity of X sub-system. And if things like anomalous Rotes that defy the rules are wanted as part of Mage, let's aknowledge them as anomalous and let's include the concept into the setting and the rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-05-2024, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:58:33-08:00","id":1532023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1531977#post1531977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would want, first and foremost, a streamlined and consistent spheres system, with the spheres having similar and easily understandable progressions and purviews. If spheres can't have the same progression then similar spheres should have similar progressions. There should be generalized rules that cover commonly occurring permutations like locking effects and setting conditions, that are easy to understand and give an indication of how to approach more niche situations. It should be clear that the game rules are game rules, not in universe metaphysics. If the magic system is done right, it shouldn't need to take up so much of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fully agree with this. Though I'd take it one step further, and try to make the Spheres more modular, so that players who want to fine-tune what their mages can do with their Magick have the option to do so, and the book doesn't attach a stigma to it. This could be done by, e.g., allowing a mage to focus on a particular purview of a Sphere instead of learning the whole thing, or by letting a mage learn specific rotes without necessarily having the Spheres that would otherwise be needed to cast them. <br /> <br /> Though this sort of thing wouldn't <i>necessarily</i> be something to put in the core book. I could, for instance, see \u201crote learning\u201d presented in an M30 Guide to the Technocracy; the study of Purviews in addition to Spheres presented in an M30 Guide to the Traditions; and maybe even alternate organizing principles like a modern-day version of DA:Mage's Foundation and Pillars presented in an M30 Guide to the Disparates. That said, these customization options would be designed to build on the Magick system found in the M30 core book, and would be presented as <i>strictly optional</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1531977#post1531977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After that, I'd focus on fleshing out the character of the setting. The various places (the Digital Web, High Umbra, etc) should be described as characters in their own right, with a focus on how they feel and why they are important. Breathe life into the world and make it a place the characters want to visit. That also includes the Ascension War itself. It's not a place, but it heavily impacts places and I'd like to see more focus on the fallout and strangeness it unleashes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also agreed. Note that this should be more than just \u201cwhat Otherworldly realms exist in the setting?\u201d \u2014 though that's an important part of it. I'd also like to see a sort of travelogue that gives a rundown on what the Ascension War looks like on each region of the Earth, with Reality Zones playing a more significant role in this: don't just say what a Technocratic Reality Zone is; give a few examples of some Technocratic Reality Zones. Likewise with each of the other types of Reality Zones. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1531977#post1531977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think its time to go back to the drawing board on the Traditions. I don't mean throw them out entirely, but many of them have origins that are incompatible with the groups they represent, usually because those origins are based on modern occult groups rather than real historical groups (or believable fictional ones). Remove those odd origins and let the Traditions be more like who they are meant to represent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also think that it's time to go back to the drawing board on the Traditions. But I think that the first and most important decision to be made is: should the Traditions be stand-ins for Focus? In the first three editions of the game, if you wanted to play a monotheistic Mage, the default assumption was that you'd do so by selecting the Celestial Chorus as his Tradition; and from that, you'd get his Theory and Practice of Magick. As such, the Celestial Chorus needed to be envisioned as a suitable home for any monotheist. And one of the most problematic elements of the Celestial Chorus was that it <i>wasn't</i> presented in that way: it was presented as a pseudo-Theosophic group with Christian trappings. <br /> <br /> But if M30 replaces Traditions with Focus as the thing that determines what kind of mage you are, then it's not as important that the Celestial Chorus be representative of all monotheists. Indeed, the fact that they <i>don't </i>represent the typical monotheist and instead represent a pseudo-Theosophic cult becomes a <i>distinguishing feature</i> of the Celestial Chorus, a reason why a monotheistic mage might look at the organization and say \u201cthanks, but no thanks\u201d. <br /> <br /> That said, this sort of detail is the sort of thing I'd want an M30 Guide to the Traditions to cover; it's far too much detail for the core book to get into. I'd much rather the core book pay attention primarily to Focus and Spheres; and to the extent that it pays attention to the Ascension War, it should do so on the level of the Technocracy, the Council of Magick, the Disparates, the Nephandi, and the Marauders, <i>not</i> on the level of the individual Tradition, Convention, or Craft. Let Focus handle that. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T08:07:51-08:00","id":1532030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532020#post1532020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> said.<br /> <br /> To add to that &quot;streamlined and consistent spheres system&quot;, there are several &quot;sub-systems&quot; that also could use that treatment. Wonders could use to be more streamlined and consistent.<br /> <br /> As they are now, examples are often inconsistent with how the creation system works. Wonder creation rules, and the Background costs associated, can be very obscure even in those times they're consistent, being hard to understand even for those of us that read the book several times. To say the least. I was able to understand some things thanks to these Forums after discussing what I had read several times. And even then I have many doubts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. I like how <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> handled this: rather than there being a separate \u201cWonders\u201d system, it has a means of channeling magic through items; and it has a further means of making this permanent by expending a dot of Willpower. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532020#post1532020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Altrough much less obscure, Countermagick it's also odd. It's not clear to me if it's an application of Spheres like any other (that would require Focus and such), or if it's an inherent power of Mages. It doesn't follow the general rules (it can't be deduced from the Sphere system that a lvl 1 on a Sphere would &quot;impede&quot; another mage's effect, and the difficulty isn't consistent). Because of that it's not transparent to me that one can extrapolate or permutate to use with other aspects of the system (Can I lower it's Diff with Quint? - I guess not) .</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I like <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s approach to this: the Arcana have Attainments, which are things that the Arcana can do without having to cast a spell; and Counterspell is a one-dot Attainment, meaning that having one dot in an Arcanum lets you engage in Countermagic without having to cast a spell. <br /> <br /> Frankly, M30 would do well to borrow heavily from Awakening's magic system, just retooled to reflect <b>Ascension</b>'s principles of Magick. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532020#post1532020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps more than &quot;streamlined&quot; the word that I would want to use it's &quot;clear&quot;. Altrough that would likely require the former.<br /> <br /> No more &quot;hidden rules&quot; that need to be deduced from Rotes, or some particular sub-system, because the authors seem to assume them (since they're found repeatedly) but can't be deduced from the general system. Let the particular be deductible from the general every time that would be possible, and when it isn't let's be clear that this is a particularity of X sub-system. And if things like anomalous Rotes that defy the rules are wanted as part of Mage, let's aknowledge them as anomalous and let's include the concept into the setting and the rules</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T10:13:44-08:00","id":1532047,"title":"","content":"Something else to consider would be to ditch the Nature and Demeanor system that <b>Mage</b> inherited from <b>Vampire</b>, and to replace it with something that reinforces <b>Mage</b>'s themes. For example: make the Paradigms serve as a way of recovering Willpower. Once per scene, if you act in a manner consistent with your Paradigm, you gain a point of Willpower. Or perhaps tie Willpower recovery to the Avatar Essences, in a manner similar to how <b>Werewolf</b> lets characters regain Willpower through their Auspices. If that's too broad, maybe make it part of the Resonance system instead: whenever you act in accordance with your strongest Resonance, you earn a point of Willpower. Just as a few of the possibilities. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd like a mix of Paradigm and Avatar Essence, if only because those are two supposedly core elements of a character design that completely lack any associated game systems. Given that they're supposed to be central to the mage's personality, they could do with some system support.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T15:59:21-08:00","id":1532065,"title":"","content":"I like Nature/Demeanor as a psychosocial dynamic. But linking Willpower to Paradigm is brilliant. A person with a <b>Caregiver </b>nature using acts of caring to reinforce their Paradigm would be profoundly logical. Picture a <b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bJester </b>demeanor <b>Visionary </b>nature using witty jokes to disrupt someone's closeminded worldview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T12:05:18-08:00","id":1532093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532020#post1532020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What [USER=&quot;758&quot;]No more &quot;hidden rules&quot; that need to be deduced from Rotes, or some particular sub-system, because the authors seem to assume them (since they're found repeatedly) but can't be deduced from the general system. Let the particular be deductible from the general every time that would be possible, and when it isn't let's be clear that this is a particularity of X sub-system. And if things like anomalous Rotes that defy the rules are wanted as part of Mage, let's aknowledge them as anomalous and let's include the concept into the setting and the rules</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Offhand these are the sections I think are most needed:<br /> <br /> Locking, this time with specific guidelines.<br /> <br /> Basic rules for making a spell able to detect things after it is cast. Wards and time triggers, at the very least, need to be able to do this.<br /> <br /> Basic rules for when there's an apparent need to include a sphere, but the spell isn't altering or transmuting the domain of that sphere. The example I can think of right now is isolating a spell to a bacteria or toxin inside someone's body.<br /> <br /> <br /> To avoid people assuming rules that are not there, I'd also want the following made explicit:<br /> <br /> You don't need pattern spheres to target spells at a pattern. You only need them to target part of a pattern. That is, a mage can teleport a rock without Matter, but he can't teleport half a rock without Matter.<br /> <br /> If you don't need Matter to affect an object with a spell, you don't need Life to affect a creature with a spell.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, two sphere abilities that are hinted at but really need to be explained:<br /> <br /> Correspondence 2's Thicken Space was apparently supposed to allow it to create Minor Wards, but there's no way to read that ability from the Corr 2 writeup. This needs explanation and limits.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 has some kind of animating or foundational capacity that appears to be the basis of animating the inanimate and/or breathing life into illusions. It's not clear how this works so its not clear when you would use it.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T12:19:55-08:00","id":1532095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532023#post1532023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fully agree with this. Though I'd take it one step further, and try to make the Spheres more modular, so that players who want to fine-tune what their mages can do with their Magick have the option to do so, and the book doesn't attach a stigma to it. This could be done by, e.g., allowing a mage to focus on a particular purview of a Sphere instead of learning the whole thing, or by letting a mage learn specific rotes without necessarily having the Spheres that would otherwise be needed to cast them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I very much agree, especially as rotes don't have that much of a purpose in Ascension so they are otherwise wasted wordcount. It wouldn't take too much space to give some rote rules and the possibility of a reduced cost for a sphere for a reduced purview. Actual variant spheres should probably wait for a supplement, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532023#post1532023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also agreed. Note that this should be more than just \u201cwhat Otherworldly realms exist in the setting?\u201d \u2014 though that's an important part of it. I'd also like to see a sort of travelogue that gives a rundown on what the Ascension War looks like on each region of the Earth, with Reality Zones playing a more significant role in this: don't just say what a Technocratic Reality Zone is; give a few examples of some Technocratic Reality Zones. Likewise with each of the other types of Reality Zones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, that is what I was going for. A full cosmology is a better fit for an expansion. I would include quick descriptions of the various Umbrae and realms with a focus on why they matter and what value they might have for the players. I hadn't thought of applying the same philosophy to earthly reality zones, but it is a really good idea.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm not interested in is a clear answer on how malleable reality is. Which is to say, I have strong opinions on the matter, but I don't think that the game line is served by having a clear answer. Honestly its an esoteric matter that doesn't impact most games. I'd probably duck the issue with a simple statement like: &quot;It can range anywhere from complete mutability to a completely defined base reality. The default assumption is somewhere in the middle. Mages in universe don't really know either, though like players they can have very strong opinions on the matter.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532023#post1532023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that it's time to go back to the drawing board on the Traditions. But I think that the first and most important decision to be made is: should the Traditions be stand-ins for Focus? In the first three editions of the game, if you wanted to play a monotheistic Mage, the default assumption was that you'd do so by selecting the Celestial Chorus as his Tradition; and from that, you'd get his Theory and Practice of Magick. As such, the Celestial Chorus needed to be envisioned as a suitable home for any monotheist. And one of the most problematic elements of the Celestial Chorus was that it <i>wasn't</i> presented in that way: it was presented as a pseudo-Theosophic group with Christian trappings.<br /> <br /> But if M30 replaces Traditions with Focus as the thing that determines what kind of mage you are, then it's not as important that the Celestial Chorus be representative of all monotheists. Indeed, the fact that they <i>don't </i>represent the typical monotheist and instead represent a pseudo-Theosophic cult becomes a <i>distinguishing feature</i> of the Celestial Chorus, a reason why a monotheistic mage might look at the organization and say \u201cthanks, but no thanks\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your idea. It doesn't address all of the issues I have with the Traditions history, but it addresses other issues I wasn't really considering. What do you envision a typical Tradition being like then, and how does it come about? How much of a change is this?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T18:21:12-08:00","id":1532131,"title":"","content":"I'm mainly thinking that most of the discrepancies between a given Tradition and the practitioners that it's supposedly based on remain, but as \u201chow the Tradition is different\u201d. By contrast, I'd work hard to make sure that the Paradigms and Practices more faithfully reflect the styles of magic that they're supposed to represent. So, taking Faith and the Celestial Chorus as examples, the Practice of Faith should be written up to *ahem* faithfully represent how typical devotees of major world religions such as Christianity would see what Mage calls Willworking; meanwhile, the Celestial Chorus is a Tradition based on a pseudo-Theosophic philosophy that has <i>claimed </i>to speak for all monotheists in the past; though that's held a significant dose of hypocrisy that until recently was tolerated out of the necessity of joining a Tradition in order to benefit from the Council of Magick. <br /> <br /> My own vision of the new Council of Magick would be one that has abandoned the \u201cNine Seats\u201d model: in the past, when that was in place, mages who only kind of fit into a given Tradition's beliefs often had to bite their tongues in order to have representation on the Council; but without the Nine Seats model, and with a more innovative \u201copen representation\u201d model facilitated by the likes of the Mercurial Elite, the new Council has seen the old Traditions lose a lot of their former influence as individual mages can contribute to council business more directly. It ceases to be \u201cThe Council of Nine Mystical Traditions\u201d, and simply becomes \u201cThe Council of Magick\u201d. <br /> <br /> Basically, the Traditions are still there; but they're the \u201cold guard\u201d. The new generation of the Council of Magick embrace a much more individualistic arrangement. This does a couple of things: it lets you keep the Traditions in the game, but portray them in a less flattering light than earlier editions did and also make them optional; while at the same time, it enables you to portray the Ascension War more directly as individualists on the Council's side vs. conformists on the Technocracy's side, if you want to. And it does so by letting you downplay the paradox of the supposedly individualistic side operating in groups. <br /> <br /> Alternately, it lets you play <i>up</i> the new conflict between the old-time Traditionists and the new wave of independent mages, with the former struggling to maintain relevancy while the latter struggle to deal with the unintended consequences that come with ditching the structure that the Traditions provide. <i>Can</i> this new vision of a Tradition-free Council work? Or will the experiment fail, with the Traditions eventually reasserting their authority when it is shown that some level of organization and structure is needed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T07:29:02-08:00","id":1532160,"title":"","content":"I agree that rotes as they currently exist seem superfluous beyond describing what can be done with sphere combinations. For a more tangible rote either they should let you employ a paradigm appropriate ability roll instead of just a raw arete roll, provide some form of outside assistance (like invoking a spirit, thoughtform, mythic thread, etc.) that provide additional benefits/reduced requirements, or both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T09:05:46-08:00","id":1532165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532131#post1532131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mainly thinking that most of the discrepancies between a given Tradition and the practitioners that it's supposedly based on remain, but as \u201chow the Tradition is different\u201d.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Alternately, it lets you play <i>up</i> the new conflict between the old-time Traditionists and the new wave of independent mages, with the former struggling to maintain relevancy while the latter struggle to deal with the unintended consequences that come with ditching the structure that the Traditions provide. <i>Can</i> this new vision of a Tradition-free Council work? Or will the experiment fail, with the Traditions eventually reasserting their authority when it is shown that some level of organization and structure is needed?</div> </div> </div> </div>So its not that there needs to be a Tradition for every major group, but that a much larger percentage of mages are members of The Traditions without being members of a Tradition? I think that's a good way to build upon what's already in Mage to make the factions more reasonable. I could even see a trial bicameral test run going on. Something akin to a Senate/House split or House of Lords/House of Commons split. One council represents the official Traditions, the other represents the individual members or the Chantries.<br /> <br /> I still think the modern occult roots should be downplayed in the history of the Traditions too. Partly because it often turns unintentionally offensive to real world cultures and religions and partly as a matter of verisimillitude. I don't want to keep picking on the Choristers but they are the easiest example. Their history is incoherent because they are somehow both a heretical faction that would be persecuted if they were ever found out, and the faction responsible for persecuting heresy. That's an admittedly simplistic explanation, but its a refrain I run into every time I look at their history.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean removing those influences, it means demoting them to subgroups of the Tradition. There can still be a strong Theosophical sect within the Chorus, it could even be that it had such a rise of prominence due to modern Theosophism that it became the face of the Chorus for a while, but it just doesn't make sense as the core identity of the Chorus.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T09:55:42-08:00","id":1532168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532165#post1532165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So its not that there needs to be a Tradition for every major group, but that a much larger percentage of mages are members of The Traditions without being members of a Tradition?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I'm thinking, yes. In fact, one thing that I think M20 goofed on was placing the Orphans under the Disparates: for M30, I'd list them under the Traditions \u2014 albeit as \u201cIndependent Mages\u201d, with \u201cOrphans\u201d recast as a derogatory nickname for them. As M20 presents it, you get the sense that the percentage of independent mages within the Traditions is zero; and it shouldn't be. I'd want <i>at least</i> a tenth, and possibly as much as half, of the Traditionists of the M30 setting to be Independent. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532165#post1532165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's a good way to build upon what's already in Mage to make the factions more reasonable. I could even see a trial bicameral test run going on. Something akin to a Senate/House split or House of Lords/House of Commons split. One council represents the official Traditions, the other represents the individual members or the Chantries.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u2026or like the Security Council and the General Assembly of the United Nations. <br /> <br /> Maybe not individual Chantries; but I could see the \u201csecond chamber\u201d being organized by geographic region rather than by, well, Tradition. <br /> <br /> And where the Council of Traditions is concerned, we could add a \u201cTenth Seat\u201d that's intended to represent the Independent Mages as a whole. Essentially, the Council of Magick's counterpart to the Order of Hermes' House Ex Miscellanea. And like House Ex Miscellanea, there would be difficulties associated with this Independent Seat, such as how well the seat-holder can speak for, or even speak <i>to</i>, a bunch of mages who by definition have no unifying identity. Though on the other hand, the mere <i>presence</i> of the Seat would act as a constant reminder to the others that there <i>are</i> mages in the Traditions who are Independent. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532165#post1532165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think the modern occult roots should be downplayed in the history of the Traditions too. Partly because it often turns unintentionally offensive to real world cultures and religions and partly as a matter of verisimillitude. I don't want to keep picking on the Choristers but they are the easiest example. Their history is incoherent because they are somehow both a heretical faction that would be persecuted if they were ever found out, and the faction responsible for persecuting heresy. That's an admittedly simplistic explanation, but its a refrain I run into every time I look at their history.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean removing those influences, it means demoting them to subgroups of the Tradition. There can still be a strong Theosophical sect within the Chorus, it could even be that it had such a rise of prominence due to modern Theosophism that it became the face of the Chorus for a while, but it just doesn't make sense as the core identity of the Chorus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Just keep in mind that it's not as important to try to make the individual Traditions \u201call-inclusive\u201d of the broad types of mages that they supposedly represent; and in fact, it makes some sense for them to have beliefs and policies that could easily turn away a prospective mage who might at first glance seem like a decent fit. Which has the benefit that you can make them more cohesive, because they no longer have to represent potentially contradictory takes on a particular type of mage. Sticking with the Choristers for now (because, as you mentioned, they're the easiest example), you can keep the \u201cecumenicism above all else\u201d notion mentioned in their chapter in <b>Lore of the Traditions</b>; but instead of saying that otherwise suitable mages who leave the Celestial Chorus over this leave the Traditions entirely and instead to over to the Templars, say that a significant number of them remain with the Traditions as Independent mages: they don't have a problem with the Traditions as a whole, just with the Celestial Chorus in particular. <br /> <br /> And so something similar with each of the other Traditions: find something that provides a specific identity for that Tradition, and have mages who share that Tradition's preferred Practices but who don't fit its core identity exist as Independents instead. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T10:20:17-08:00","id":1532170,"title":"","content":"Just going reiterate the Rogue Council/Emissaries of the Sphinx already exist and with more fleshing out would be the natural fit for the tenth Tradition and Tradition mages who don't quite fit in the existing nine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T11:04:54-08:00","id":1532175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532168#post1532168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. Just keep in mind that it's not as important to try to make the individual Traditions \u201call-inclusive\u201d of the broad types of mages that they supposedly represent; and in fact, it makes some sense for them to have beliefs and policies that could easily turn away a prospective mage who might at first glance seem like a decent fit. Which has the benefit that you can make them more cohesive, because they no longer have to represent potentially contradictory takes on a particular type of mage. Sticking with the Choristers for now (because, as you mentioned, they're the easiest example), you can keep the \u201cecumenicism above all else\u201d notion mentioned in their chapter in <b>Lore of the Traditions</b>; but instead of saying that otherwise suitable mages who leave the Celestial Chorus over this leave the Traditions entirely and instead to over to the Templars, say that a significant number of them remain with the Traditions as Independent mages: they don't have a problem with the Traditions as a whole, just with the Celestial Chorus in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I agree with that part. In fact the 'ecumenism above all else' is something that would push quite a number of mages away from the Chorus and is nevertheless a good fit for the Tradition, especially if it comes packaged with a push to ignore core tenets and dogmas in the name of working together or understanding God. For a philosophy more based more around a shared approach, the general sense that peeling back the layers of reality will reveal the face of the divine could work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Becksworth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532170#post1532170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just going reiterate the Rogue Council/Emissaries of the Sphinx already exist and with more fleshing out would be the natural fit for the tenth Tradition and Tradition mages who don't quite fit in the existing nine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how meshed M30 wants to be with history, they could even be the spark for that second chamber.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T12:31:24-08:00","id":1532179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532175#post1532175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, I agree with that part. In fact the 'ecumenism above all else' is something that would push quite a number of mages away from the Chorus and is nevertheless a good fit for the Tradition, especially if it comes packaged with a push to ignore core tenets and dogmas in the name of working together or understanding God. For a philosophy more based more around a shared approach, the general sense that peeling back the layers of reality will reveal the face of the divine could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Expanding this beyond just the Celestial Chorus, it might be appropriate for <i>all</i> of the Traditions to have something akin to an \u201cecumenicism\u201d element to them: to me, <i>the</i> thing that distinguishes the Traditions as a whole from the Disparates is their shared belief that they're all doing the same thing. And they hold this view to such an extent that if a Verbena, a Son of Ether, and a Chorister decide to work together on a single collaborative Effect, <i>they can. </i>But it comes at the cost that they have to at least partially water down their own views of what Magick is, in order to allow for the possibility that this radically different thing that Joey over there is doing is somehow compatible with it. <br /> <br /> Independent Traditionists and Disparates wouldn't necessarily but into that \u2014 which <i>would</i> mean that they might have a bit more difficulty with cooperative Effects; but this might be balanced with them being more effective on their own or with others who share their views. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532175#post1532175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on how meshed M30 wants to be with history, they could even be the spark for that second chamber.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Whatever the Rogue Council started out as, its current incarnation could very well be \u201cthe Tenth Tradition\u201d. And having a Bodhisattva of Correspondence involved could certainly reduce the issue I mentioned before of how they might speak for/to such an incoherent constituency. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T13:17:22-08:00","id":1532184,"title":"","content":"In Ascension they basically left off with the Emissaries basically pushing hard for the 10th seat right as the end game begins, but that plot point was basically dropped in 20th, presumably in favor of the Disparate Alliance.<br /> <br /> For the Disparates, part of the appeal I feel was the conspirtorial uncertainty of the alliance. Are Traditions and Technocracy both under Nephandi control? In that case what Crafts can be trusted? I would want a separate guide for the Alliance detailing there dozens of potential crafts, giving the GM plenty of options to work as the players are on the ground floor of establishing the Alliance and sussing out who can be trusted in joining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T13:48:26-08:00","id":1532190,"title":"","content":"For me, the most appealing aspect of the Disparates is their drive for authentic experience, and their unwillingness to compromise on that. Unlike the Traditions, they <i>don't </i>necessarily buy into the idea that \u201cwe're all doing the same thing\u201d; to the extent they share a common view on why different magical beliefs work, it tends to be \u201cagnostic\u201d: \u201cwe know how our Magick works, and we know <i>that</i> other Magicks work, too; but we <i>don't care why.</i>\u201d They're not trying for all-encompassing magical beliefs that explain anything and everything, including other magick; they just want to stay true to their own beliefs. The two biggest exceptions to this are the Batini (who would love nothing better than to get the Disparates to accept the same \u201cit's all one and the same\u201d view that the Traditions hold) and the Hollow Ones (who practice Gutter Magick and don't really <i>have</i> a unified set of Magickal beliefs that they pursue). <br /> <br /> And the result is that the Disparate Alliance is an alliance of convenience, where each Craft is given some role to play in the overall organization and everyone is expected to stay in their own lanes and out of each other's ways. At this point, the only thing holding them together is their shared concern about Nephandi infiltration, adding a level of paranoia to them that's not particularly suited for long-term trust-building. <br /> <br /> Another result of this \u201cstay in your own lane\u201d arrangement is that there isn't really any room in the Disparate Alliance for independent mages. The Hollow Ones are about as close as you get; and that's more a matter of the \u201cwhatever works\u201d nature of their Gutter Magick than it is about actual independence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T14:42:30-08:00","id":1532197,"title":"","content":"In terms of making the Magick system better, one thing I'd like to do would be to make it a bit more responsive to the mage's beliefs. <br /> <br /> I mentioned <b>Prism of Focus</b> before. One of the things that book does is to add structure to Paradigms by posing a series of questions for each Paradigm to answer, along with a set of possible answers for each (called Tenets): for instance, \u201cHow does the Universe Work?\u201d (A Rational Universe; As Above, So Below; Fall from Grace; Reality is a Lie; The Divine is Real; Unfathomable Forces at Work); \u201cWhy can I use Magick?\u201d (I am Chosen; I am not limited; I am special; I have greater understanding); and \u201cWhat is the point of it all?\u201d (Achieve Full Knowledge; Annihilation is Freedom; Build a Utopia; Existence is Meaningless; Merge with the Divine; Power is its own reward). One of the questions asked is called the Epistemological question: how is knowledge acquired? (Mystical Insights, Scientific Experimentation, Divine Revelations).<br /> <br /> If M30 includes something like this, it might have the mage's answer to this question influence how Magick works, possibly in a manner similar to the Technomancer/mystic divide in M20: If you choose Mystical Insights, you have the option to Work Without Focus; but your Arete is capped by your Willpower. If you choose Scientific Experimentation, you can't Work Without Focus, but you also don't face any restrictions on your use of Magick beyond the need for it to conform to your Practices. If you choose Divine Revelation, you tend to experience Wild Magick (representing whatever higher power you serve working through you); but you're susceptible to Faithlessness (failing to uphold your divine benefactor's will can result in access to your Magick being blocked until you atone). <br /> <br /> That won't work for <i>every</i> Tenet; it may not even work for <i>most</i> of them. But I could see something <i>like</i> this, if used sparingly, making it easier to represent seemingly contradictory belief systems in a common set of rules for Magick. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T16:00:43-08:00","id":1532201,"title":"","content":"In terms of independent mages and where they would fit best, that still seems like a &quot;it depends&quot; situation to me. Like a mage that is effectively in a micro-craft (ex: a Shinto shrine family with their own unique practices specific to their one shrine) might fit best in the Disparate Alliance should they deign to get involved in larger mage politics. A mentor-student lineage that is independent from but has links to the Traditions would probably continue to deal with Tradition politics to some extent, even if their practices have diverged over generations. Meanwhile, true Orphan whose focus is wholely self made/taught might garner the usual suspicion Orphans get no matter where they go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5286-becksworth","name":"Becksworth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T07:23:15-08:00","id":1532239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532197#post1532197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of making the Magick system better, one thing I'd like to do would be to make it a bit more responsive to the mage's beliefs.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> If M30 includes something like this, it might have the mage's answer to this question influence how Magick works, possibly in a manner similar to the Technomancer/mystic divide in M20: If you choose Mystical Insights, you have the option to Work Without Focus; but your Arete is capped by your Willpower. If you choose Scientific Experimentation, you can't Work Without Focus, but you also don't face any restrictions on your use of Magick beyond the need for it to conform to your Practices. If you choose Divine Revelation, you tend to experience Wild Magick (representing whatever higher power you serve working through you); but you're susceptible to Faithlessness (failing to uphold your divine benefactor's will can result in access to your Magick being blocked until you atone).<br /> <br /> That won't work for <i>every</i> Tenet; it may not even work for <i>most</i> of them. But I could see something <i>like</i> this, if used sparingly, making it easier to represent seemingly contradictory belief systems in a common set of rules for Magick.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll add a potential feature to the Divine Revelation version. Some religions have elements whose effectiveness is based on the faith or moral state of the practitioner and others that always work regardless of those states. There are also many where time honored rituals and collective prayer have special effect. Without taking a deep dive into comparative religion, this is another thing that could potentially be adapted to the rote system. Faithlessness or certain externals could increase the difficulty of improvisational casting, but not for rotes or ritual casting. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T11:58:23-07:00","id":1532442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If M30 includes something like this, it might have the mage's answer to this question influence how Magick works, possibly in a manner similar to the Technomancer/mystic divide in M20: If you choose Mystical Insights, you have the option to Work Without Focus; but your Arete is capped by your Willpower. If you choose Scientific Experimentation, you can't Work Without Focus, but you also don't face any restrictions on your use of Magick beyond the need for it to conform to your Practices. If you choose Divine Revelation, you tend to experience Wild Magick (representing whatever higher power you serve working through you); but you're susceptible to Faithlessness (failing to uphold your divine benefactor's will can result in access to your Magick being blocked until you atone).<br /> <br /> That won't work for <i>every</i> Tenet; it may not even work for <i>most</i> of them. But I could see something <i>like</i> this, if used sparingly, making it easier to represent seemingly contradictory belief systems in a common set of rules for Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this, but considering the many and very different types of beliefs and Focus ... and altrough it migth be a bit complex ... this could also be systematized as a sort of &quot;metamagick&quot; that can be aproved by the ST<br /> <br /> Create a table with the things about the system &quot;belief&quot; can change. Things like &quot;can cast w/o focus&quot;, &quot;experience Wild Magick&quot;, &quot;increase/decrease difficulty, successes, etc&quot;...whatever helps.<br /> <br /> This way, people can design their own &quot;Mystic vs. Terchnomancer&quot; divides using their own criteria about what being, say, Faithless means. Heck, even while the &quot;metamagick table&quot; ain't likely to cover every posibility, it would be easier to houserule new ones if we had a table with several &quot;modules&quot; to use as sample<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Since we`re on the subject of Divine Revelation, it always bugged me a little that people that have a magical system that involves external powers that &quot;know things&quot; (or has a personal take on what &quot;knowing&quot; means) has to still obey the rule about needing to know what you create in order to create it. Like, how one needs to know tons about economy and how money it's made to make a &quot;real&quot; dollar bill.<br /> <br /> So, what if my chorister with Prime 2/Matter 3 want's one bill and asks a favor from above ... doesn't God know what I'm asking for?. What about the spirits?, I'm asking the spirit of Dollars to create one for me, with all the Spheres you want, why do ***I*** need to know the particulars of how dollars are made?.<br /> <br /> To ignore this requisite in exchange of other problems (Wild Magick could be it, since you're relying on external powers, and if these know things they likely have agency too) could be one of these","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T05:41:42-07:00","id":1532563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1531973#post1531973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">20th Anniversary editions were, for the most part, compilations of the previous editions, which lead to massive tomes that tried to fit everything into one book. For a 30th Anniversary Edition, I'd prefer something that <i>doesn't </i>try to fit everything in one book: plan to do a series of supplements to flesh out what the core book can't handle, and swim for the core book to be comparable to the size of M2 or MRev.</div> </div> </div> </div>I myself am of the completely opposite mind. The very reason why I like the 20th editions is precisely because it has everything that I need compacted in a single book, rather than spread out towards 20+ dusty tomes. I like supplements to be SUPPLEMENTS rather than &quot;basically essentials&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, I think that this format actually condenses the content in a much better way. Were it otherwise, it would get far more extensive and filled with filler - like it was with 2e or Rev. Because you end up having to have the Basic Book, then the Guide to the Trads, then the Guide to the Techies, then the &quot;Storytellers Handbook&quot; and the &quot;Forged in Dragons'Fire&quot; and &quot;Guide to the Nephandi&quot; and &quot;Guide to the Marauders&quot; and &quot;Guide to the Crafts&quot; and on and on and on, and each one of those would contain a lot of filler for the real important stuff contained on each.<br /> <br /> With the 20th editions, it is all compact and a lot more &quot;to the point&quot; than in any previous editions. And I don't need to keep the list of references of 20+ books for the information I want.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T05:54:52-07:00","id":1532564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1531977#post1531977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would want, first and foremost, a streamlined and consistent spheres system, with the spheres having similar and easily understandable progressions and purviews. If spheres can't have the same progression then similar spheres should have similar progressions. There should be generalized rules that cover commonly occurring permutations like locking effects and setting conditions, that are easy to understand and give an indication of how to approach more niche situations. It should be clear that the game rules are game rules, not in universe metaphysics. If the magic system is done right, it shouldn't need to take up so much of the book.<br /> <br /> After that, I'd focus on fleshing out the character of the setting. The various places (the Digital Web, High Umbra, etc) should be described as characters in their own right, with a focus on how they feel and why they are important. Breathe life into the world and make it a place the characters want to visit. That also includes the Ascension War itself. It's not a place, but it heavily impacts places and I'd like to see more focus on the fallout and strangeness it unleashes.<br /> <br /> I also think its time to go back to the drawing board on the Traditions. I don't mean throw them out entirely, but many of them have origins that are incompatible with the groups they represent, usually because those origins are based on modern occult groups rather than real historical groups (or believable fictional ones). Remove those odd origins and let the Traditions be more like who they are meant to represent.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I answered Dataweaver before because it was in the sequence of posts, but THIS is what I would want for ANY Mage Edition above ALL ELSE.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bBefore describing any new cool kid in Trads or Techies or the new cool Chess Club of Mages that is quicking everybody else's ass, before any of that, I want a Sphere system upon which they just don't throw random nonsensical stuff because &quot;it feels right&quot;.<br /> <br /> I want Spheres to state very clearly what they can do at each level;<br /> Sphere of Awesomeness:<br /> Lvl 1 - detect Awesome<br /> Lvl 2 - fiddle with Awesomeness<br /> Lvl 3 - Manipulate Awesoness<br /> Lvl 4 - Great Awesome Manipulation<br /> Lvl 5 - Turn boring into Awesome.<br /> <br /> Then I want that basic description to become the uttermost and FINAL blueprint for ANY effects - AKA Forces 3, Prime 2, Awesome 3 - create Awesome Fire Balls.<br /> <br /> I don't want any of the nonsensical &quot;a hurricane is Forces 4, a breeze is Forces 2&quot;. If they do come with this idiocy again, then I WILL demand of them to tell me exactly from what amount of Joules does wind manipulation goes from &quot;minor&quot; to &quot;major&quot; forces, or the maximum possible Voltage and Amperage that I can conjure for a lightning with Forces 3. I want that garbage gone.<br /> <br /> That to me is the most important thing above all else for a new edition (which is obviously not going to be M5 of course)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T06:12:53-07:00","id":1532569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1531979#post1531979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the pre-M20 editions, your choice of Tradition largely determined how you're Magick looks, such that if you wanted to play a witch, you did it by making a Verbena. M20 took what had previously been the Theory and Practice sections of the Tradition write-ups and made them stand-alone choices of Paradigms and Practices under the new Focus section; so now, if you want to play a witch, you make a mage with the Practice of Witchcraft. If your mage isn't engaging in Council politics, there's no longer any need for her to be a Verbena.<br /> <br /> In M30, I'd love to take that further: instead of each Tradition getting a two-page write-up and a position in the book that suggests that you pretty much have to choose a Tradition, I'd give each Paradigm and Practice a half-page spread (again, like Prism of Focus), and I'd reduce the Traditions, Conventions, and Crafts to two paragraph sketches, one of which would be akin to the Focus paragraph for the faction that's found in M20. Put more detailed write-ups for <i>all</i> of them in supplements: an M30 Guide to the Traditions, an M30 Guide to the Technocracy, and an M30 Guide to the Disparates. But you shouldn't need <i>any</i> of them to play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may sound silly now, but the Trads of the very 1ed were nothing short of the &quot;classes&quot; of D&amp;D. Which is why some are a bit peculiar.<br /> <br /> For instance:<br /> <br /> Wizards = Order of Hermes<br /> Druids = Verbena<br /> Shamans = Dreamspeakers<br /> Necromancers = Euthanatos<br /> Monks = Akashics<br /> Clerics = Celestial Chorus<br /> <br /> The other 3 are more original thou (Etherboys, 1990's-dance-music-VAs and the Seers of the Ecstasy).<br /> <br /> I am... Still not sure about the rest thou. I mean, ok, the idea of playing an Hermetic techmancer is awesome... Or a &quot;Techno-Shaman&quot; Dreamspeaker, or a &quot;Witchcraft-Scientist&quot; Etherite... I like all of those. But I still think they should keep their core Paradigms... For instance, an Etherite can practice &quot;Witchcraft&quot;, but only insofar as they view by the prism of &quot;Da sCience!&quot;, or in other words, instead of thinking that &quot;it is the will of Da Mother&quot;, it is instead &quot;quantum fluctuations of psionic vibrations&quot; technobabble","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T06:20:26-07:00","id":1532570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Becksworth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1531993#post1531993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, one thing I would have liked to gave seen was some new modern day crafts or sub tradition group. Perhaps you could flesh out the Emissaries of the Sphinx as the new prospective 10th tradition and give them some inventive new sub groups and practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing I absolutely would NOT want to see is even more &quot;clans&quot;. WoD their &quot;clans&quot; splats, and I always hated them.<br /> <br /> I loved when VtM used to be 7 clans only, with another 6 &quot;theoretical/mysterious&quot; ones, but then came the &quot;Guide to players&quot; and &quot;Guide to Sabbath&quot; which introduced not only the remaining 6, but also a plethora of bloodlines, and that trend spread out throughout all of WoD.<br /> <br /> One of the things I liked about WtA is that they managed to stick to 13 tribes, even thou they did attempt over the years to create a few &quot;bloodlines&quot; for the Garou (but they compensated this with the addition of the many Fera).<br /> <br /> I think we already have more than enough splats and sub-splats as it is, and anything additional should be left for the players","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T06:28:26-07:00","id":1532571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532047#post1532047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else to consider would be to ditch the Nature and Demeanor system that <b>Mage</b> inherited from <b>Vampire</b>, and to replace it with something that reinforces <b>Mage</b>'s themes. For example: make the Paradigms serve as a way of recovering Willpower. Once per scene, if you act in a manner consistent with your Paradigm, you gain a point of Willpower. Or perhaps tie Willpower recovery to the Avatar Essences, in a manner similar to how <b>Werewolf</b> lets characters regain Willpower through their Auspices. If that's too broad, maybe make it part of the Resonance system instead: whenever you act in accordance with your strongest Resonance, you earn a point of Willpower. Just as a few of the possibilities.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd like a mix of Paradigm and Avatar Essence, if only because those are two supposedly core elements of a character design that completely lack any associated game systems. Given that they're supposed to be central to the mage's personality, they could do with some system support.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an outstanding idea. Paradigm, Essence and Resonance should have more impactful mechanics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T07:01:27-07:00","id":1532574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532095#post1532095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I very much agree, especially as rotes don't have that much of a purpose in Ascension so they are otherwise wasted wordcount. It wouldn't take too much space to give some rote rules and the possibility of a reduced cost for a sphere for a reduced purview. Actual variant spheres should probably wait for a supplement, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Over the years I have played with these ideas. To the point that my &quot;Hedge Magicians&quot; don't use the &quot;official Disciplines&quot; of the many Sorcerors supplements, they instead buy individual Rotes, and they can learn those from Awakened Mages.<br /> <br /> I let players &quot;buy Rotes&quot; as well known spells. The advantage is that they can use those with a lot more bang than &quot;versatile Magic&quot; done on the spot. And, because I get Rotes on levels, they can even go above their Avatar rating. <br /> <br /> I've also have been already using alternative Spheres and Sub Spheres for years. It works wonderfully and I have to say that it is so much better to play a Pyromancer, a Shapeshifter or a Plant Druid than a Life/Forces Mage.<br /> <br /> The problem that I found here is about the XP costs. The Storyteller system is hard to fiddle with XP costs, because the difference between &quot;7 x current level&quot; to &quot;6 x current level&quot; is both massive and not enough. So my solution was to &quot;Gurps-iffy&quot; these costs, which works incredibly well for me and my tables, but wouldn't work for the system. But that was what allowed me to distribute the Spheres of Necromancy, Plant-Magic, Empathy-Magic and to allow my players to also buy individual &quot;static&quot; Rotes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indeed, that is what I was going for. A full cosmology is a better fit for an expansion. I would include quick descriptions of the various Umbrae and realms with a focus on why they matter and what value they might have for the players. I hadn't thought of applying the same philosophy to earthly reality zones, but it is a really good idea.<br /> <br /> One thing I'm not interested in is a clear answer on how malleable reality is. Which is to say, I have strong opinions on the matter, but I don't think that the game line is served by having a clear answer. Honestly its an esoteric matter that doesn't impact most games. I'd probably duck the issue with a simple statement like: &quot;It can range anywhere from complete mutability to a completely defined base reality. The default assumption is somewhere in the middle. Mages in universe don't really know either, though like players they can have very strong opinions on the matter.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Agreed 100%. I for one envision the WoD as a Gnostic setting as &quot;Da Truth&quot;, but that's MY VISION for it, which I prefer it to be the way I see it without being necessarily &quot;da truth&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the Cosmology, I was creating a Umbra to resemble the human mind; I still haven't finished it, but it got interesting. I envisioned a distinction between our neurology and our psychology, so the &quot;neurological Umbra&quot; would be like the &quot;Natural Umbra&quot; that shapeshifters are more used to, while the &quot;Psychological Umbra&quot; would be more of the theme park of Mages, and I connected to dots from there. For example, the Underworld of the Dead would be the MEMORY. &quot;Hell&quot; or whatever you wanna call places of Ctonic forces, would be a representation of the Jungian concept of the Shadow, but they are also a manifestation of the Freudian idea of ID; the &quot;Astral Plane&quot; I envisioned as a sort of &quot;membrane&quot; that connects all of the Umbra, and represents the &quot;Pre Conscious Mind&quot; - aka not exactly what you are conscious about, but what you CAN be conscious about - for instance, you may not be thinking about what you just ate for breakfast, but if I ask you what it was, you can quickly conjure it to your conscious mind. Dark thoughts aren't always present in our conscious mind either, but they simply &quot;pop up&quot; into our consciousness seemingly out of nowhere. Thus, the &quot;Astral Plane&quot; is the main method of travel in this version of Umbra of mine, and it connects all the Realms inside it. The Penumbra represents the most superficial part of the Conscious Mind, connected to our senses, thus it is what we see and hear and smell and feel. Then the &quot;Middle Umbra&quot; would be the subconscious, and the &quot;Deep Umbra&quot; holds all the Jungian Archetypes.<br /> <br /> In this representation, the Material Plane represents our body, thus it is &quot;outside&quot; of the mind in a way, and beyond the Umbra lies the Qlipphotic, which represents the &quot;outside&quot; or &quot;exterior world&quot;.<br /> <br /> I did this based on this Gnostic concept, thus reframing the Umbra as &quot;God's mind&quot;, although it can still be used without that being necessarily true. <br /> <br /> That's just an idea, but it could give some direction towards a cosmology that makes some sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T07:18:36-07:00","id":1532575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532197#post1532197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of making the Magick system better, one thing I'd like to do would be to make it a bit more responsive to the mage's beliefs.<br /> <br /> I mentioned <b>Prism of Focus</b> before. One of the things that book does is to add structure to Paradigms by posing a series of questions for each Paradigm to answer, along with a set of possible answers for each (called Tenets): for instance, \u201cHow does the Universe Work?\u201d (A Rational Universe; As Above, So Below; Fall from Grace; Reality is a Lie; The Divine is Real; Unfathomable Forces at Work); \u201cWhy can I use Magick?\u201d (I am Chosen; I am not limited; I am special; I have greater understanding); and \u201cWhat is the point of it all?\u201d (Achieve Full Knowledge; Annihilation is Freedom; Build a Utopia; Existence is Meaningless; Merge with the Divine; Power is its own reward). One of the questions asked is called the Epistemological question: how is knowledge acquired? (Mystical Insights, Scientific Experimentation, Divine Revelations).<br /> <br /> If M30 includes something like this, it might have the mage's answer to this question influence how Magick works, possibly in a manner similar to the Technomancer/mystic divide in M20: If you choose Mystical Insights, you have the option to Work Without Focus; but your Arete is capped by your Willpower. If you choose Scientific Experimentation, you can't Work Without Focus, but you also don't face any restrictions on your use of Magick beyond the need for it to conform to your Practices. If you choose Divine Revelation, you tend to experience Wild Magick (representing whatever higher power you serve working through you); but you're susceptible to Faithlessness (failing to uphold your divine benefactor's will can result in access to your Magick being blocked until you atone).<br /> <br /> That won't work for <i>every</i> Tenet; it may not even work for <i>most</i> of them. But I could see something <i>like</i> this, if used sparingly, making it easier to represent seemingly contradictory belief systems in a common set of rules for Magick.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my God, I absolutely loved this idea! I'll try to make a table for it right away!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T05:17:31-07:00","id":1532765,"title":"","content":"1) Different art style please. I really dislike that of M20. I mean its fine if its in a book about orphans or the virtual adepts and so on, but other than that, its too flamboyant, too much, i am not sure what the word is. My favourite is that of very late revised. The last two technocracy books. Having said that, i also dislike an art style dominating an entire edition. For instance, surealism does very much fit infernalism books imo.<br /> <br /> 2) No writing Tradition books based on &quot;what would i, the writer, want them to do, think of them, if i was forced to be, say, an Euthanatos, a Hermetic, An Etherite etc. Actually, the same concept for the gameline as a whole. Do not take sides in the various conflicts, internal or otherwise (Intra-tradition, the traditions as a whole, the Ascension War, etc)<br /> <br /> 3) Overall, i am very cynical with regards to how power corrupts. In this sense, i always played Ascension with some elements of Awakening, even before i read the latter game. (No wisdom chart though, please!)<br /> <br /> 4) At least, give an option to use pillars, if you so prefer. Expand on them, write some rotes with both spheres and them, etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T07:57:25-07:00","id":1532807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532765#post1532765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Different art style please. I really dislike that of M20. I mean its fine if its in a book about orphans or the virtual adepts and so on, but other than that, its too flamboyant, too much, i am not sure what the word is. My favourite is that of very late revised. The last two technocracy books. Having said that, i also dislike an art style dominating an entire edition. For instance, surealism does very much fit infernalism books imo.<br /> <br /> 2) No writing Tradition books based on &quot;what would i, the writer, want them to do, think of them, if i was forced to be, say, an Euthanatos, a Hermetic, An Etherite etc. Actually, the same concept for the gameline as a whole. Do not take sides in the various conflicts, internal or otherwise (Intra-tradition, the traditions as a whole, the Ascension War, etc)<br /> <br /> 3) Overall, i am very cynical with regards to how power corrupts. In this sense, i always played Ascension with some elements of Awakening, even before i read the latter game. (No wisdom chart though, please!)<br /> <br /> 4) At least, give an option to use pillars, if you so prefer. Expand on them, write some rotes with both spheres and them, etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, no more writing with active malice towards parts of the system or the fanbase: Avoid glib explanations like &quot;Can you roll more successes than God?&quot; and &quot;Seriously, this is a truly stupid spell.&quot; No making up new rules to make something you don't like harder. No wasting word count making it clear how very much you do not like the thing. (The Notorious Vampiric Lawn Chair should be a field guide for how not to write Mage, HDYDT's Co-Location section is quite bad too).<br /> <br /> If the fanbase has recurring systems disputes, the writers need to take the time to understand both sides before weighing in. Otherwise they are just wasting wordcount and not actually helping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T09:59:32-07:00","id":1532809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532807#post1532807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, no more writing with active malice towards parts of the system or the fanbase: Avoid glib explanations like &quot;Can you roll more successes than God?&quot; and &quot;Seriously, this is a truly stupid spell.&quot; No making up new rules to make something you don't like harder. No wasting word count making it clear how very much you do not like the thing. (The Notorious Vampiric Lawn Chair should be a field guide for how not to write Mage, HDYDT's Co-Location section is quite bad too).<br /> <br /> If the fanbase has recurring systems disputes, the writers need to take the time to understand both sides before weighing in. Otherwise they are just wasting wordcount and not actually helping.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, i am against easy transformation of Kindred into humans (Isn't this where &quot;outroll god&quot; came from?) Likewise some spells do need structure.<br /> <br /> But the lawnchair example stands. I thought i was being trolled when i read it lol<br /> <br /> whats wrong with the co-location spells ?I have not read them ? Its correspondence 4 or 5, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T10:58:31-07:00","id":1532812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532809#post1532809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, i am against easy transformation of Kindred into humans (Isn't this where &quot;outroll god&quot; came from?) Likewise some spells do need structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>No disagreements there, but &quot;Can you outroll God?&quot; is a snarky way of conveying that. While I will admit, I laughed and found it helpful when I read it, many found it antagonistic and in hindsight I agree with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> whats wrong with the co-location spells ?I have not read them ? Its correspondence 4 or 5, right? </div> </div> </div>The Spacial Mutation and Co-Location sections of HDYDT are a hot mess of absurdly high success costs, made up rules, and running commentary (&quot;Such things make Storytellers (and game designers) seek out other lines of work.&quot;). There's no consistency between the costs of effects either, which is particularly problematic when the point of the book is to help understand the rules. <br /> <br /> Transposing locations in particular has a success cost of 10 successes per layer + 10 successes per quarter mile + 1 success per 10 minutes (but, for some reason, is unaffected by distance or familiarity), gives the mage 5 Paradox points per 10 minutes of the effect, is not affected by modifiers. It overrides at least three of the standard parts of the magic system, and one of the examples it gives costs something like 70 successes, when 'godlike' feats are supposed to be ~20.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T14:24:54-07:00","id":1532818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532812#post1532812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No disagreements there, but &quot;Can you outroll God?&quot; is a snarky way of conveying that. While I will admit, I laughed and found it helpful when I read it, many found it antagonistic and in hindsight I agree with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Spacial Mutation and Co-Location sections of HDYDT are a hot mess of absurdly high success costs, made up rules, and running commentary (&quot;Such things make Storytellers (and game designers) seek out other lines of work.&quot;). There's no consistency between the costs of effects either, which is particularly problematic when the point of the book is to help understand the rules.<br /> <br /> Transposing locations in particular has a success cost of 10 successes per layer + 10 successes per quarter mile + 1 success per 10 minutes (but, for some reason, is unaffected by distance or familiarity), gives the mage 5 Paradox points per 10 minutes of the effect, is not affected by modifiers. It overrides at least three of the standard parts of the magic system, and one of the examples it gives costs something like 70 successes, when 'godlike' feats are supposed to be ~20.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>wait what? 5 paradox per 10 minutes?? 70 successes??? Even creating a rank 5 node takes only 50 lol. You might as well say &quot;Don't do that, lol&quot; would have been more honest.<br /> <br /> The only cases where i accept special paradox rules is, say, something like Czar Vargo. Something that &quot;must&quot; go wrong, else the world as we know it changes. E.g. transforming the President into a pig in front of a 1000 cameras, should, conceivably, come with some sort of backlash.<br /> <br /> But this? I don't get why. Its a pretty &quot;core&quot; part of correspondence.<br /> I have nerfed abilities before, for various reasons including a relative 'balancing' but i am not sure what the point is<br /> <br /> Reminds me of the ludicrous system given for conjuring money. I mean, what if my character has a less technocratic paradigm?<br /> What if i am just asking the spirits? What if i view money/cars/etc as platonic ideals??<br /> To an extend i get it, mind you, but its far fetched. Someone took a reasonable concept, existing even for blood mages, and multiplied by a factor of 10 or so.<br /> <br /> Once again, just say that its impossible. Would have been more honest..<br /> <br /> Do i need Science 3 in order to conjure a fireball? Does creating a sword requite craft(4) ?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Since we are talking about wish lists..<br /> i wish there were a bit fewer abilities... Jetpack?? Seriously?? Does my Taftani need &quot;Magic Carpet&quot;? or, say, the laser weapon one.. Yes, very reasonable,, i will be adding &quot;Magic Wand&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Also, less cinematic martial arts system please. Someone looked at the KotE Storyteller companion, stole some surprisingly balanced abilities, and buffed them to infinity. I do Martial Arts in rl, a bit anyway, and i am almost insulted , lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T15:43:17-07:00","id":1532819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532818#post1532818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, less cinematic martial arts system please. Someone looked at the KotE Storyteller companion, stole some surprisingly balanced abilities, and buffed them to infinity. I do Martial Arts in rl, a bit anyway, and i am almost insulted , lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Cinematic martial arts absolutely _should_ be possible \u2014 but only by applying Magick. Coincidental Magick (due to Hypernarratives); but still Magick. It is, conceptually, what Magick Enhancing Abilities exists for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T18:11:46-07:00","id":1532831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532812#post1532812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No disagreements there, but &quot;Can you outroll God?&quot; is a snarky way of conveying that. While I will admit, I laughed and found it helpful when I read it, many found it antagonistic and in hindsight I agree with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Spacial Mutation and Co-Location sections of HDYDT are a hot mess of absurdly high success costs, made up rules, and running commentary (&quot;Such things make Storytellers (and game designers) seek out other lines of work.&quot;). There's no consistency between the costs of effects either, which is particularly problematic when the point of the book is to help understand the rules.<br /> <br /> Transposing locations in particular has a success cost of 10 successes per layer + 10 successes per quarter mile + 1 success per 10 minutes (but, for some reason, is unaffected by distance or familiarity), gives the mage 5 Paradox points per 10 minutes of the effect, is not affected by modifiers. It overrides at least three of the standard parts of the magic system, and one of the examples it gives costs something like 70 successes, when 'godlike' feats are supposed to be ~20.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The comment regarding God would not really work depending on the Paradigm of the mage. I think this is most apparent in Paradigms where the mage is God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T04:43:50-07:00","id":1532842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532819#post1532819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no. Cinematic martial arts absolutely _should_ be possible \u2014 but only by applying Magick. Coincidental Magick (due to Hypernarratives); but still Magick. It is, conceptually, what Magick Enhancing Abilities exists for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, this is what i meant. No cinematic martial arts, using the Martial arts/brawl ability alone.<br /> <br /> I am not even saying it should require true magick. Martial arts sorcery paths could well exist.<br /> And of course, DO for the Akashikc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T05:06:47-07:00","id":1532843,"title":"","content":"I don't think that Do should be \u201ccinematic martial arts without Magick\u201d; I think it should be \u201ccinematic martial arts through the use of Magick as Focused by the Akashayana\u201d. It shouldn't necessarily need <i>much</i> Magick; and depending on how the M30 Magick system works, it might not even require an Arete roll: I could see M30's version of Magick Enhancing Abilities having an option that allows an appropriate set of prerequisites to unlock special uses for Abilities that aren't normally available to them, for instance; and Do Maneuvers would be an example of that. But it would be the sort of thing where you'd need to have a Do-centered Focus and either one or two dots in appropriate Spheres before you're allowed to use the Do Maneuvers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T05:12:18-07:00","id":1532844,"title":"","content":"Conceptually, I'd like M30's Magick Enhancing Abilities to resemble Exalted's Charms, though without the need to acquire them one at a time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T08:31:35-07:00","id":1532860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532844#post1532844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conceptually, I'd like M30's Magick Enhancing Abilities to resemble Exalted's Charms, though without the need to acquire them one at a time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean having a few specific modes (excellencies) like difficulty reduction, extra successes that are the base approach before you go into more specific effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T14:59:28-07:00","id":1532872,"title":"","content":"Not necessarily, although something to the effect of Excellencies is part of what I'm thinking of. I <i>do</i> think that would come first, in the sense that the Sphere rank needed to unlock it ought to be the first dot; but I don't see that as being presented as a <i>prerequisite</i> for the rest, conceptually. <br /> <br /> What I'm <i>really</i> thinking about would be things like Wise Arrow (or perhaps \u201cBullet Bending\u201d in the modern world), Wound-Cleansing Meditation, or Motive-Discerning Technique: your Arete and Spheres <i>enable</i> a supernatural feat; but the actual roll to make it happen is an Ability-based pool. (There would, of course, need to be some sort of trade-off to this, or else everyone would be doing it all the time.)<br /> <br /> Actually, I'm not sure how much of this would be Magick Enhancing Abilities and how much would be Abilities Enhancing Magick, or if it even matters; my point is that I'd like to see the Magick system pay a bit more attention to the notion of using Magick and Abilities together to achieve extraordinary or supernatural results, with the Coincidental version of this being the enabler of cinematic feats.<br /> <br /> These aren't new capabilities that Magick hasn't been able to do before; they'd be a simpler and more streamlined way of using those capabilities \u2014 something that doesn't require multiple actions and a sequence of rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T05:52:17-07:00","id":1532902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532872#post1532872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily, although something to the effect of Excellencies is part of what I'm thinking of. I <i>do</i> think that would come first, in the sense that the Sphere rank needed to unlock it ought to be the first dot; but I don't see that as being presented as a <i>prerequisite</i> for the rest, conceptually.<br /> <br /> What I'm <i>really</i> thinking about would be things like Wise Arrow (or perhaps \u201cBullet Bending\u201d in the modern world), Wound-Cleansing Meditation, or Motive-Discerning Technique: your Arete and Spheres <i>enable</i> a supernatural feat; but the actual roll to make it happen is an Ability-based pool. (There would, of course, need to be some sort of trade-off to this, or else everyone would be doing it all the time.)<br /> <br /> Actually, I'm not sure how much of this would be Magick Enhancing Abilities and how much would be Abilities Enhancing Magick, or if it even matters; my point is that I'd like to see the Magick system pay a bit more attention to the notion of using Magick and Abilities together to achieve extraordinary or supernatural results, with the Coincidental version of this being the enabler of cinematic feats.<br /> <br /> These aren't new capabilities that Magick hasn't been able to do before; they'd be a simpler and more streamlined way of using those capabilities \u2014 something that doesn't require multiple actions and a sequence of rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it would fit some paradigms, but i am afraid of consequences. Like, how far do we go with &quot;What a human can do, but better&quot;? <br /> At the very least, i would not allow replication of feats beyond, say, terrestrial martial arts level of strength? Essence 2 solar charms?<br /> Remember that the solars are the premier tier for a reason. <br /> Still, the idea is not a bad one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T06:34:36-07:00","id":1532904,"title":"","content":"My references to Exalted are intended to be inspirational, not prescriptive: that is, I'm not talking about incorporating the specifics of Exalted Charms into Mage; I'm talking about having Mage do something similar in concept. An NWO Agent with two(?) dots in Correspondence ought to be able to bend the trajectory of his bullets around obstacles; though that should be Vulgar. And, more importantly, there should be a way to do it without having to make a separate Arete roll and a Firearms roll. Likewise with a ninja running across a field of snow and not leaving footprints, or a witch providing an herbal remedy that works as well as modern pharmacy drugs do. <br /> <br /> Basically, what I'm advocating is a mechanism whereby your Focus plus the right traits (usually Spheres) serve as a gateway to using Abilities in unusual ways, without having to go through the process of making an Arete roll to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T08:26:23-07:00","id":1532908,"title":"","content":"I could see where instead of an Arete and an Ability roll a mage might use an Arete+Ability roll. So that NWO agent would be able to bend bullets with an Arete+Firearms roll, the ninja an Arete+Athletics roll, and the witch an Arete+Herbalism(?) roll. <br /> <br /> We would need a good system for determining when this is possible, preferably one we could summarize quite quickly. My intuition is that this should only apply to fast casting, not rituals. I also think this could explode if it also applies to skill based attacks that roll magical damage (fire punches, etc). Playtesting could determine if either of those are issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T11:39:51-07:00","id":1532916,"title":"","content":"Arete+Medicine. The fact that it's herbalism comes from the fact that she's Practicing Witchcraft; and in the context of witchcraft, Medicine often involves herbs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T12:25:10-07:00","id":1532918,"title":"","content":"Also, the Arete+Ability pool might be a neat alternative to separate Arete and Attribute+Ability rolls without being inherently superior to it, depending on how the former is implemented. As an example, take the bullet-bending: as separate rolls, you'd roll your Arete to activate the bullet-bending, then you'd roll Dexterity+Firearms to hit your target, for two actions. As a single, combined roll, you'd be rolling Arete+Firearms with a difficulty of the higher of the two, and <i>then you split the successes </i>between allowing the bullet-bending and hitting the target. <br /> <br /> The advantage is that you don't need to take two actions to pull this off; the drawback is that it's harder to pull off, because the dice pool is trying to do two things at once: add a magical Effect to an otherwise mundane use of an Ability, and the otherwise mundane use of the Ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-20T15:31:26-07:00","id":1532923,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I would not be opposed to a soft reboot of Mage: The Ascension, though I imagine that what I would look for in a reboot is not what Paradox Interactive would look for in it. Mainly, I think Mage could be benefitted by emphasizing Paradigms, removing the Consensus, and having the Traditions by replaced by individual magical groups. I do expect there to be something of a divide between Awakened mages and sorcerers, but there should still be some overlap. The Consensus is mainly troublesome as it effectively renders every model of the universe equally incorrect. Mages can still be united by the fact that they are miracle-workers, but there should still be objectivity to individual paradigms. In particular, it would be nice to see actual debates and cosmological battles between groups. If anything, this would only add to the drama of the Ascension War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T10:39:15-07:00","id":1532947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verlan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532923#post1532923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I would not be opposed to a soft reboot of Mage: The Ascension, though I imagine that what I would look for in a reboot is not what Paradox Interactive would look for in it. Mainly, I think Mage could be benefitted by emphasizing Paradigms, removing the Consensus, and having the Traditions by replaced by individual magical groups. I do expect there to be something of a divide between Awakened mages and sorcerers, but there should still be some overlap. The Consensus is mainly troublesome as it effectively renders every model of the universe equally incorrect. Mages can still be united by the fact that they are miracle-workers, but there should still be objectivity to individual paradigms. In particular, it would be nice to see actual debates and cosmological battles between groups. If anything, this would only add to the drama of the Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some legitimate problems with the idea of the Consensus, especially when the books blur the lines between what the Traditions believe and what the metaphysics of the game are. However, the world needs to stay malleable for the Ascension War to make sense.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest instead going back to 2nd edition where humans weren't the only thing that contributed to the Consensus, spirits and other entities have an impact, the structures of the High Umbra influence how the world thinks, etc. Let there be multiple fronts that the war can be fought on and multiple ways of influencing the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T13:18:46-07:00","id":1532955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532947#post1532947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are some legitimate problems with the idea of the Consensus, especially when the books blur the lines between what the Traditions believe and what the metaphysics of the game are. However, the world needs to stay malleable for the Ascension War to make sense.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest instead going back to 2nd edition where humans weren't the only thing that contributed to the Consensus, spirits and other entities have an impact, the structures of the High Umbra influence how the world thinks, etc. Let there be multiple fronts that the war can be fought on and multiple ways of influencing the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem is that the nature of the Consensus prevents any given cosmology from actually being correct. Instead of having people trying to present the virtues of their models in explaining the universe, you have individuals trying to change reality to fit their philosophies. If you know that your Paradigm is only correct because you believe in it, then you cannot actually meaningfully believe in it. A person with a cosmology that includes God would almost certainly just want to be correct about the universe from the get go. It is very unlikely that they would want to change the universe so that God exists. <br /> <br /> Also, you are correct in that if the Consensus is included, non-human entities should be able to affect it. As an aside, the structure of the Umbra could be improved upon. It feels too defined and disconnected from real-world religions and occult traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T13:53:34-07:00","id":1532961,"title":"","content":"Speaking from experience, that's exactly the wrong way to go. This is exactly what happened when Mage: the Awakening came out. And if you like that approach to the game, I highly recommend trying Awakening.<br /> <br /> But the removal of the ability to shape reality to your wishes was off-putting for many Ascension fans. Attempting to do that in M30 would have a similar negative effect.<br /> <br /> The most that should be done along those lines is to keep the notion of Earthly Foundations, so that mages who want to fight for what is really true as opposed to attempting to impose their idea of Truth on reality can make the argument that what they're fighting for is consistency with the Earthly Foundations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T14:05:40-07:00","id":1532962,"title":"","content":"Very few mages think that what they believe is only correct because they believe in it. The ones that do are usually Marauders. <br /> <br /> Most mages think that their paradigms are correct. Most of them are aware that other paradigms work as well to a greater or lesser extent. Physical reality also seems to push back against certain paradigms, some more than others. This seems to track at least somewhat to the beliefs of the unawakened. <br /> <br /> There are numerous opinions on what this means.<br /> <br /> 1) It might mean, as you say, that nothing is real and everything is only true if it is believed in. <br /> <br /> 2) It might mean that there is a singular truth that mages are approaching as they get closer to Ascension, and all the beliefs of mages and the world are pieces of that greater truth. That's a popular one among the Traditions.<br /> <br /> 3) It might mean that the powers of mages are somehow alien to the world and warp reality into something it shouldn't be. I can see that one being popular in particularly hardline Technocrats.<br /> <br /> 4) It might mean that the world is vast and complex and these various paradigms are true and actually work with each other, but no one can see enough to see how. That's likely another popular Traditions one.<br /> <br /> 5) It might mean that belief shapes how people perceive a very complex reality, that changing the consensus doesn't change reality just how it is seen. <br /> <br /> The list goes on.<br /> <br /> M30 would likely be best served by establishing that mages don't know the full truth and have a variety of arguments about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T14:52:00-07:00","id":1532964,"title":"","content":"I <i>do</i> think M30 would be better if the notion that \u201cMagick is imposing your beliefs on reality\u201d was downgraded from \u201cthis is the objective Truth\u201d to \u201cthis is what the Traditions believe\u201d; so that the options that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> just mentioned can potentially <i>be </i>the truth, rather than being misunderstandings that mages have before they eventually realize that it's all really just a matter of wishing hard enough. <br /> <br /> That is: on an out of character level, leave the fundamental nature of Magick undefined, with the explanation given in previous editions being <i>one possibility</i> that the Storyteller can choose to be true if he wants it to be. Talk about what evidence mages have about what the ultimate truth might be, and offer several options for the Storyteller to choose among; but avoid explicitly answering the question even on the meta-level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T15:55:09-07:00","id":1532966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532961#post1532961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking from experience, that's exactly the wrong way to go. This is exactly what happened when Mage: the Awakening came out. And if you like that approach to the game, I highly recommend trying Awakening.<br /> <br /> But the removal of the ability to shape reality to your wishes was off-putting for many Ascension fans. Attempting to do that in M30 would have a similar negative effect.<br /> <br /> The most that should be done along those lines is to keep the notion of Earthly Foundations, so that mages who want to fight for what is really true as opposed to attempting to impose their idea of Truth on reality can make the argument that what they're fighting for is consistency with the Earthly Foundations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer Ascension over Awakening; the latter felt like it wanted to model some sort of contemporary fantasy setting of its own construction. Specifically, I think it would be best for Ascension to retain the ability to cover all sorts of characters, from mad scientists to magicians and more. In Awakening, you are very much always reminded that you are playing within the Awakening setting. With Ascension, you feel like you are playing a game where you play a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T16:06:40-07:00","id":1532969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532962#post1532962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very few mages think that what they believe is only correct because they believe in it. The ones that do are usually Marauders.<br /> <br /> Most mages think that their paradigms are correct. Most of them are aware that other paradigms work as well to a greater or lesser extent. Physical reality also seems to push back against certain paradigms, some more than others. This seems to track at least somewhat to the beliefs of the unawakened.<br /> <br /> There are numerous opinions on what this means.<br /> <br /> 1) It might mean, as you say, that nothing is real and everything is only true if it is believed in.<br /> <br /> 2) It might mean that there is a singular truth that mages are approaching as they get closer to Ascension, and all the beliefs of mages and the world are pieces of that greater truth. That's a popular one among the Traditions.<br /> <br /> 3) It might mean that the powers of mages are somehow alien to the world and warp reality into something it shouldn't be. I can see that one being popular in particularly hardline Technocrats.<br /> <br /> 4) It might mean that the world is vast and complex and these various paradigms are true and actually work with each other, but no one can see enough to see how. That's likely another popular Traditions one.<br /> <br /> 5) It might mean that belief shapes how people perceive a very complex reality, that changing the consensus doesn't change reality just how it is seen.<br /> <br /> The list goes on.<br /> <br /> M30 would likely be best served by establishing that mages don't know the full truth and have a variety of arguments about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an extent, I think that was also more of a problem with the 20th Anniversary Edition. I think the problem is that for gameplay purposes, True Magic has to be differentiated from True Faith, Psychic Phenomena, and Hedge Magic, even though under the mage's Paradigm, their magic may fall into one of those categories. It reminds me of how the description for a Paradigm based on psychic phenomena specifically mentioned that your character is not actually using psychic abilities, and that their powers worked because they believed that it worked. I do not think that all parts of Mage are so heavy-handed with it, but it is still present in the background. Furthermore, parts of the cosmology of Mage limits what sorts of Paradigms a mage can meaningfully have. For example, Gilgul would not work in every cosmology, particularly in ones that hold the Avatar to be a soul. There is the continuing problem in Mage where the pragmatic concerns of game mechanics tend to trump the actual magical traditions involved. Your Avatar cannot be your Atman if it can be destroyed. That simply does not work in the cosmology in question. If anything, reality is not really up for grabs in Mage. There cannot really be a situation where you were right all along. No matter your Paradigm, you will somehow have to make it fit under the baked-in cosmology. You have to contend with the Tellurian, Avatar Essences, the Pure Ones, the list goes on. Ascension ultimately suffers from the same problem of Awakening; its basic premise is hamstrung by the cosmology that is built around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-21T16:13:48-07:00","id":1532970,"title":"","content":"That's a necessary consequence of establishing a single truth and sticking to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T06:20:23-07:00","id":1533000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532964#post1532964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>do</i> think M30 would be better if the notion that \u201cMagick is imposing your beliefs on reality\u201d was downgraded from \u201cthis is the objective Truth\u201d to \u201cthis is what the Traditions believe\u201d; so that the options that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> just mentioned can potentially <i>be </i>the truth, rather than being misunderstandings that mages have before they eventually realize that it's all really just a matter of wishing hard enough.<br /> <br /> That is: on an out of character level, leave the fundamental nature of Magick undefined, with the explanation given in previous editions being <i>one possibility</i> that the Storyteller can choose to be true if he wants it to be. Talk about what evidence mages have about what the ultimate truth might be, and offer several options for the Storyteller to choose among; but avoid explicitly answering the question even on the meta-level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. And it is actually possible to give multiple frameworks for the words &quot;Magic is imposing your beliefs on reality,&quot; but it requires more nuance and more wordcount. Making it a Traditions specific idea, or better yet one specific to some in the the Traditions would let the writers convey other ideas more easily and quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T11:42:43-07:00","id":1533012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532964#post1532964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>do</i> think M30 would be better if the notion that \u201cMagick is imposing your beliefs on reality\u201d was downgraded from \u201cthis is the objective Truth\u201d to \u201cthis is what the Traditions believe\u201d; so that the options that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> just mentioned can potentially <i>be </i>the truth, rather than being misunderstandings that mages have before they eventually realize that it's all really just a matter of wishing hard enough.<br /> <br /> That is: on an out of character level, leave the fundamental nature of Magick undefined, with the explanation given in previous editions being <i>one possibility</i> that the Storyteller can choose to be true if he wants it to be. Talk about what evidence mages have about what the ultimate truth might be, and offer several options for the Storyteller to choose among; but avoid explicitly answering the question even on the meta-level.</div> </div> </div> </div>1)Do be fair, even on a meta- level, it is not usually defined as &quot;just&quot; imposing belief. Else the very use of instruments would be unnecessary to begin with.<br /> I prefer to think that you are imposing belief through a certain framework that exists.whether due to the pure ones or the Consensus or the One, or or..<br /> <br /> 2)Even Porthos does not just say &quot;i am imposing belief&quot; He has merely internalized the elements of his paradigm ( Ok the hermetics love to say that, but its obviously more complex than that. Or at least this is how i personally choose to interpret it.)<br /> <br /> 3)One alternative would be what the Order of Reason told the Outer Labyrinth : &quot; Hey guys, yes, imposition of will like the Hermetics do is possible, but our thing works based on scientific laws and so will-working is not part of it&quot; <br /> But its hard to imagine a Mage that does not at least say&quot; Look, imposition of Will is at least part of what you are doing,&quot;<br /> <br /> 4)Maybe Dark ages Mage is the correct answer ? TO paraphrase &quot; In this era magic is seen as something external. Even those who are most focused on will-working than everyone else believe that they are accessing an external thing : the emanations of magic itself&quot;<br /> <br /> 5) Though, to be honest, i was always of the opinion that few mages are obsessively pro &quot; Its willpower only and there is ZERO, nilch, nada outside me thinking about it&quot; <br /> Its actually mage players, who most have this opinion rather than the various books explaining metaphysics. That is, its a literal reading of the Core Rules that causes the problem<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T12:19:25-07:00","id":1533013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1533012#post1533012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)Do be fair, even on a meta- level, it is not usually defined as &quot;just&quot; imposing belief. Else the very use of instruments would be unnecessary to begin with.<br /> I prefer to think that you are imposing belief through a certain framework that exists.whether due to the pure ones or the Consensus or the One, or or..<br /> <br /> 2)Even Porthos does not just say &quot;i am imposing belief&quot; He has merely internalized the elements of his paradigm ( Ok the hermetics love to say that, but its obviously more complex than that. Or at least this is how i personally choose to interpret it.)<br /> <br /> 3)One alternative would be what the Order of Reason told the Outer Labyrinth : &quot; Hey guys, yes, imposition of will like the Hermetics do is possible, but our thing works based on scientific laws and so will-working is not part of it&quot;<br /> But its hard to imagine a Mage that does not at least say&quot; Look, imposition of Will is at least part of what you are doing,&quot;<br /> <br /> 4)Maybe Dark ages Mage is the correct answer ? TO paraphrase &quot; In this era magic is seen as something external. Even those who are most focused on will-working than everyone else believe that they are accessing an external thing : the emanations of magic itself&quot;<br /> <br /> 5) Though, to be honest, i was always of the opinion that few mages are obsessively pro &quot; Its willpower only and there is ZERO, nilch, nada outside me thinking about it&quot;<br /> Its actually mage players, who most have this opinion rather than the various books explaining metaphysics. That is, its a literal reading of the Core Rules that causes the problem</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not actually encountered any Mage players who really hold that view. Pretty much everyone I have played with was greatly invested in the Paradigms of their characters. The problem is really in the core rules themselves. There is a real disconnect between the core principles of Mage and the cosmology that the game proffers up. At its core, Mage is a game about playing miracle-workers engaging in a philosophical war over reality. All of the cosmology sprinkled on top is in fact unnecessary, and can very much detract from the themes of the game. It is easy enough for the savvy player to grok Mage, and not pay too much attention to how the books actually describe it, but why would one write the books in such a manner in the first place?<br /> <br /> I think it is easier to get the point across with an example. If your mage has the Paradigm of a standard western ceremonial magician, then almost none of the setting's cosmology will work for them. The High Umbra will be the astral plane. There will probably not be a strict delineation between the Low Umbra and various heavenly afterlives. The Avatar will not be susceptible to Gilgul. The Pure Ones will likely be emanations of God. Avatar Essences will simply not fit into the Paradigm.<br /> <br /> In order to ensure that such a character would fit with the setting, compromises would have to be made, and that would damage the integrity of the character. The game is about playing will-workers with strong positions on reality. If one cannot reasonably play a character of a given Paradigm, then there is a real problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28352-verlan","name":"Verlan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T12:37:53-07:00","id":1533014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1533012#post1533012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)Do be fair, even on a meta- level, it is not usually defined as &quot;just&quot; imposing belief. Else the very use of instruments would be unnecessary to begin with.<br /> I prefer to think that you are imposing belief through a certain framework that exists.whether due to the pure ones or the Consensus or the One, or or..<br /> <br /> 2)Even Porthos does not just say &quot;i am imposing belief&quot; He has merely internalized the elements of his paradigm ( Ok the hermetics love to say that, but its obviously more complex than that. Or at least this is how i personally choose to interpret it.)<br /> <br /> 3)One alternative would be what the Order of Reason told the Outer Labyrinth : &quot; Hey guys, yes, imposition of will like the Hermetics do is possible, but our thing works based on scientific laws and so will-working is not part of it&quot;<br /> But its hard to imagine a Mage that does not at least say&quot; Look, imposition of Will is at least part of what you are doing,&quot;<br /> <br /> 4)Maybe Dark ages Mage is the correct answer ? TO paraphrase &quot; In this era magic is seen as something external. Even those who are most focused on will-working than everyone else believe that they are accessing an external thing : the emanations of magic itself&quot;<br /> <br /> 5) Though, to be honest, i was always of the opinion that few mages are obsessively pro &quot; Its willpower only and there is ZERO, nilch, nada outside me thinking about it&quot;<br /> Its actually mage players, who most have this opinion rather than the various books explaining metaphysics. That is, its a literal reading of the Core Rules that causes the problem</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, in fact, the rationale behind my earlier suggestion of modifying the Magick system based on the tenets of a mage's Paradigm. In particular, the point where I mentioned a triad of \u201cMystical Insights\u201d, \u201cScientific Experimentation\u201d, and \u201cDivine Revelations\u201d was built around this very notion, with 2 corresponding to Mystical Insights and 3 corresponding to Scientific Experimentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T12:28:45-07:00","id":1533130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1533014#post1533014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is, in fact, the rationale behind my earlier suggestion of modifying the Magick system based on the tenets of a mage's Paradigm. In particular, the point where I mentioned a triad of \u201cMystical Insights\u201d, \u201cScientific Experimentation\u201d, and \u201cDivine Revelations\u201d was built around this very notion, with 2 corresponding to Mystical Insights and 3 corresponding to Scientific Experimentation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go with more than just three. Some others might be:<br /> <br /> Touched by Fate/In Tune With the Cosmos/One With The Force - The mage consistently acts in accordance with some principle and because of this reality bends to his favor even without any conscious intent. As long as the mage upholds his principle he has the option of casting without focus, desire, or knowledge. That is, the <i>player</i> may choose to cast without the <i>character</i> knowing. Intentional magic works normally and will not be lost. This was something suggested in the Euthanatos sourcebook.<br /> <br /> Note: This is similar to Divine Revelation, but with a different twist that is applicable to a more hands off or even intentionless principle. <br /> <br /> Whatever Works/Freewheeling - The mage's choice of foci is much more open ended than normal to the point that the character is rarely without options. However, this means that the ST can and should suggest additional conditions or restrictions (this spell is at touch range rather than sight, or the target has to hear you, etc). This should be an interesting exercise between ST and player, not a punishment.<br /> <br /> A Different Point of View - Mages that are used to looking at reality through a strange lens (drugs, mathematics, time cube metaphysics, etc) might have a special way of casting. I can't think of a mechanical effect at the moment, though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T10:59:56-07:00","id":1533173,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, the trio I suggested was motivated by the \u201cScience, Faith, and Magick\u201d line that appeared on the cover of <b>Mage: the Sorcerers Crusade</b>. That said, I'm not opposed to diversifying beyond that, if a good example of a fourth option presents itself. Note, though, that these three cover a <i>lot</i> of ground on their own; and something to the effect of \u201cscientific mystic/techgnosi\u201d (a mechanism allowing you to hybridize them) potentially covers even more ground. Your \u201cTouched by Fate\u201d suggestion is basically a hybrid between Scientific Experimentation and Divine Revelation: if Fate/the Force/the Cosmos really is impersonal, but there's still a principle that you must live by in order to retain your Magick, that principle can in theory be analyzed like a set of scientific axioms. <br /> <br /> I don't know if I'd do the \u201chybrid learning styles\u201d as a Merit, the way M20 does with technomancers and mystics; I'd prefer not to, as I prefer options such as these to be built around trade-offs and freely selectable by the player, as opposed to being something that the player has to decide on the basis of a point budget. But if the hybridizing results in the strengths of the \u201cparent tenets\u201d covering for each others' weaknesses, resulting in something that's objectively better, then making it Merit-based would be warranted. <br /> <br /> Also, note that my original notion was focused on one particular set of tenets from <b>Prism of Focus</b>: the Epistemological Tenets, which are centered around how knowledge is acquired. Those aren't the only tenets presented there; they're just the ones that I have ready answers as to how mechanics might be attached. Another set of tenets had to do with the openness of your Paradigm: it may be Closed, Hierarchical, or Open. A Closed Paradigm is one that requires that everything be explainable through your worldview; a Hierarchical Paradigm assumes that your own Paradigm is better than the alternatives, but that the alternatives aren't wrong per se; and an Open Paradigm is one where the mage's Paradigm is viewed \u201cmerely\u201d as being the best choice <i>for him; </i>and that others have to find their own truth. I could see <i>that</i> somehow playing into the system for Quiet \u2014 how your character is likely to react when his Paradigm clashes with the world around him \u2014 with Closed Paradigms making you more susceptible to Denial (or whatever its M30 equivalent is) while Open Paradigms make you more susceptible to the M30 version of Madness. And Hierarchical either doesn't show a bias either way or it biases in a third direction (<i>not</i> Morbidity; if there's a third type of Quiet associated with the Openness of your Paradigm, I'd be inclined to compare it to Hubris). <br /> <br /> As well, individual Practices in <b>Prism of Focus</b> are given a Benefit and a Weakness: for Gutter Magick, the Benefit is that they're masters of doing more with less: while other Practices tend to be rather particular about what Resonances they can use in a given Effect, a Gutter Mage can put in a bit of extra work (take a bit more time) to leverage an otherwise irrelevant Resonance trait through some cobbled-together reasoning; and the Weakness is that they done get to use Unique Instruments.<br /> <br /> My point in bringing this up is that not everything in terms of customizing how Magick works needs to be done in the same way. In particular, not everything is a \u201cfourth option\u201d to Science, Faith, or Magick. Some things, while valid reasons to customize the rules, are independent factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T11:17:33-07:00","id":1533174,"title":"","content":"That's fair. I was thinking there would be other obvious methods that needed addressing but then couldn't think of many. I also admit I thought the Touched by Fate method would be different and when I was writing it up it became clear it was only a variant of your Divine Revelation. That said I also realized that I prefer the mechanics of Touched By Faith: that it opens up casting without intention or observation and that only that intentionless casting is lost when the mage transgresses. That is, that a mage on the outs can still cast deliberately by normal rules.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, actual mechanics are getting into the weeds for this thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T11:29:31-07:00","id":1533175,"title":"","content":"Agreed. That said, another reason I'd prefer to stick to a Science/Faith/Mysticism triplet (and various mixtures thereof) is to keep it from becoming bloated. When it comes to rules tweaks, I'm in the camp of \u201cthere <i>should</i> be some, because \u2018none\u2019 is too limiting; but less is more\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T12:36:05-07:00","id":1533193,"title":"","content":"Have I mentioned Resonance yet? I'd like to see it more thoroughly integrated into the rules for Paradox as well as regular Magick. For example: instead of splitting Quiet into multiple types, go back to the 1e and 2e notion that Quiet is Quiet; <i>but: </i>the form that your Quiet takes is influenced by your Resonance. And the four flavors of Resonance found in M20 stay: each type of Resonance, in addition to its specific type, is either Devotional, Elemental, Stabilizing, or Temperamental. When you've succumbed to Quiet and you're under the influence of a Temperamental Resonance, the result is akin to what MRev and M20 call Madness; when you're under the influence of a Stabilizing Resonance, your Quiet takes a form that could be characterized as what M20 calls Denial; when you're under the influence of an Elemental Resonance, your Quiet takes a form of a sort of obsession with whatever the element is; so if you're under the influence of Jhor (that is, the Elemental Resonance of Death), your Quiet takes a form of an obsession with death (M20's Morbidity). And if you're under the influence of a Devotional Resonance, your Quiet takes the form of a self-righteousness \u2014 a hubris where you believe that in the service to your cause, you can do no wrong.<br /> <br /> Quiet itself is \u201cmerely\u201d a mixture of you seeing things that aren't there and/or exaggerating the importance of things that are, and <i>not</i> seeing things that <i>are</i> there and/or downplaying their importance. Different so-called \u201ctypes\u201d of Quiet are merely the result effect of emphasizing one of these effects over the others, as influenced by your Resonance. <br /> <br /> And other kinds of Paradox similarly get informed by your Resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T21:33:37-07:00","id":1533296,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that &quot;Touched by Faith&quot; is exactly the same as &quot;Divine Revelation&quot;.<br /> <br /> A &quot;Mage&quot; that holds a &quot;Touched by Fate&quot; Paradigm could even be an atheist. Heck, traditional Buddhism is atheistic (or rather speaking, agnostic), but Buddha (the historical Siddhartha Gautama) could very well be &quot;Touched by Fate&quot;, despite preaching an agnostic religion that is borderline atheistic. <br /> <br /> I think there's strong ground for a 4th axis on this.<br /> <br /> &quot;Divine Revelation&quot; is Gnosticism at its highest form (we are all the One-God) or any one Theistic, Dualistic or Politheistic faiths (I'm a servant of the One True God / The God of Light and Goodness / The Gods of Creation).<br /> <br /> A &quot;Touched by Fate&quot; (we need perhaps a better name, semantics actually help our thinking processes, there is REAL power in words after all) could be for example for a group of people that believe that they have a genetic mutation that gives them psionic powers...<br /> <br /> That's not scientific, that's not mystic but it's also not divine revelation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T21:49:23-07:00","id":1533297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532872#post1532872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not necessarily, although something to the effect of Excellencies is part of what I'm thinking of. I <i>do</i> think that would come first, in the sense that the Sphere rank needed to unlock it ought to be the first dot; but I don't see that as being presented as a <i>prerequisite</i> for the rest, conceptually.<br /> <br /> What I'm <i>really</i> thinking about would be things like Wise Arrow (or perhaps \u201cBullet Bending\u201d in the modern world), Wound-Cleansing Meditation, or Motive-Discerning Technique: your Arete and Spheres <i>enable</i> a supernatural feat; but the actual roll to make it happen is an Ability-based pool. (There would, of course, need to be some sort of trade-off to this, or else everyone would be doing it all the time.)<br /> <br /> Actually, I'm not sure how much of this would be Magick Enhancing Abilities and how much would be Abilities Enhancing Magick, or if it even matters; my point is that I'd like to see the Magick system pay a bit more attention to the notion of using Magick and Abilities together to achieve extraordinary or supernatural results, with the Coincidental version of this being the enabler of cinematic feats.<br /> <br /> These aren't new capabilities that Magick hasn't been able to do before; they'd be a simpler and more streamlined way of using those capabilities \u2014 something that doesn't require multiple actions and a sequence of rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Do, I would like to see Men in Black using &quot;Scientific Martial Combat&quot; (Martial &quot;Combat&quot;, not &quot;Arts&quot;).<br /> <br /> And that exists in the real world by the way. Krav Maga holds something like it, but the official Scientific Martial Combat tries to be more rigorous in their approach; it's basically a profound study of the biomechanics and biophysics of the human body applied to diverse forms of combat (that goes over unarmed combat but also with the use of several kinds of weapons, including even firearms). Krav Maga for example does study ways to fight an enemy with a knife while you hold a briefcase and similar things.<br /> <br /> Just imagine &quot;Scientific Combat&quot; juiced up with Enlightened Sciences. That's also good for Etherites and VAs.<br /> <br /> I would also not be against that other traditions/crafts could have their &quot;own things&quot;. Or maybe not just simply giving each small little group their own exclusive unicorn &quot;Discipline&quot; that them alone know, but rather a bag of &quot;Do-Like&quot; skills - for example, &quot;Sacred Geometry&quot; that could be a specialty of Hermetics and Choristers (Feng Shui for the Akashics), with special perks to it, and so forth and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T22:12:11-07:00","id":1533298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1532908#post1532908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see where instead of an Arete and an Ability roll a mage might use an Arete+Ability roll. So that NWO agent would be able to bend bullets with an Arete+Firearms roll, the ninja an Arete+Athletics roll, and the witch an Arete+Herbalism(?) roll.<br /> <br /> We would need a good system for determining when this is possible, preferably one we could summarize quite quickly. My intuition is that this should only apply to fast casting, not rituals. I also think this could explode if it also applies to skill based attacks that roll magical damage (fire punches, etc). Playtesting could determine if either of those are issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to use Arete + Sphere already, because meager 3 dices of Arete is a sure recipe for constant critical failures that simply ruin the game.<br /> <br /> If the game mechanics change to Arete + Lowest Rank Sphere used in the Effect - not the NECESSARY Sphere level for the effect, but the level your Mage has of the Spheres; for instance, if your Mage has Arete 5, Life 5 and Mind 4, and for some reason he &quot;throws a spell&quot; that demands Life 3 Mind 1, he would roll: Arete 4 + the lowest rank he has between Life and Mind - which in this case, would be his Life 4, therefore he would throw Arete 5 + 4 (from Life).<br /> <br /> That has several benefits, getting away from miniscule dice pools not being the only one - for instance, you would give preference to &quot;stick to your better tricks&quot;, since even if you're rolling a &quot;spell&quot; that only requires lvl 1 on a Sphere, being a Master at that Sphere makes you better at it than someone taking their first lessons on it - heck, an Arete 3 Mage with Mind 3 would have the same dice pool than an Arete 5 Mage with Mind 1... Being that &quot;Arete&quot; would then become &quot;raw power&quot;, but the Sphere levels would translate more towards &quot;Experience in the field&quot;.<br /> <br /> With such a system implemented, then it becomes pretty straightforward to use &quot;Magik Enhancing Abilities&quot; or &quot;Abilities Enhancing Magik&quot;: whenever you're using Magik with a skill, instead of adding Spheres to the Arete roll, you add your skill level.<br /> <br /> Or even better, and I'll give an example: let's say that I'm a Techieboy with 5 dots in &quot;Scientific Martial Combat&quot; (the techie version of &quot;Do&quot;).<br /> <br /> Being proficient also in Biophysics Realm (which in an ideal world would be a &quot;sub sphere&quot; of &quot;Life&quot;, but you guys can call it &quot;Life Sphere&quot; if you're not found of &quot;sub Spheres&quot;), he knows body movement techniques that allow him to enhance all of his physical capabilities, techniques that go from proper respiration, the biomechanics of the body movement and even self hypnosis (fell free to add whatever technobabble of your choice).<br /> <br /> Well, then when he decides to punch the damn Trad really hard in the head, he uses a &quot;Biophysics&quot; (or Life) 3 effect.<br /> <br /> Our good ol' techie here has Life 4 Sphere. This sets the limit of how much of dots of &quot;Scientific Martial Combat&quot; he is able to add to his Arete roll. In this case, let's say he has Arete 4, SMC (Scientific Martial Combat) 5 and Life 4; he therefore rolls Arete 4 + 4 dots.<br /> <br /> If he only had 2 dots in SMC however, he would roll only Arete 4 + 2, despite having Life 4.<br /> <br /> Therefore, the Mage rolls the LOWEST between his lowest Sphere used in the effect and his skill trait.<br /> <br /> I think this would be a well rounded system, let me know if you all agree or not","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T23:14:12-07:00","id":1533300,"title":"","content":"<b>A. Types of Paradigm:</b><br /> <br /> 1- Divine Revelation;<br /> <br /> 2- Materialistic/Mechanicist (Scientific Method);<br /> <br /> 3- Mystical;<br /> <br /> 4- Fate (? - other, or simply &quot;Unknown&quot; or even &quot;Unknowable&quot;)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>B. Source of Power:</b><br /> <br /> 1- Internal (willwork, &quot;power of the soul&quot;, &quot;individual Godhood&quot; and so on)<br /> <br /> 2- External (Magical principles of the Cosmos, Scientific Discovery, Gifts from Spirits, Gifts from God(s) )<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>C. Openess of Paradigm:</b><br /> <br /> 1- Closed (only my view is right, whatever anybody else does follow the same principles as what I do, they just don't comprehend it the way I do) - susceptible to <b>Denial</b><br /> <br /> 2- Hierarchical (there are many ways to do Magik, but my way is BETTER) - susceptible to <b>Hubris</b><br /> <br /> 3- Open (there's many ways to do Magik, none are necessarily better than the others, my way is simply better for me, but everybody must find their own Truth) - susceptible to <b>Madness</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>D. Usage of Foci:</b><br /> <br /> 1- Strict: cannot do Magik without some Focus (which needs not to be some technomancy toy of the latest generation or the most precise sacred geometry, even a Techieboy can accomplish many feats by meditation, hiper memorization, hypnotic advanced techniques and so forth; but they are absolutely necessary)<br /> <br /> 2- Optional: Foci help to concentrate the Will / concentrate the Magical energies of the Cosmos / attract the will of the Spirits/God(s), but it is not indispensable, it is simply easier. I can see &quot;Psyonics&quot; having this particular worldview, where at most they simply place two fingers in each side of their heads and just think about what they want to happen and contract their sphincters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, with this simple table we could basically create any kind of Paradigm possible (I think). We just need to mix the items from each, for example, unionist techies would probably be A. 2 (Materialist/Mechanicist), B. 2 (External Sources), C. 1 (Closed) and D. 1 (Strict Foci)<br /> <br /> A Gnostic (Theosophical) Choristers would be A. 1 (Divine Revelation), B. 1 (Internal Source), C. 1 (Closed) and D. 2 (Optional Foci), while a Psychic would could be A. 4 (Fate or simply &quot;Unknown&quot;) but it could even be 2 (Materialistic/Mechanicist), B. 1 most likely, but a Nephandi could very well believe that his &quot;psychic powers&quot; are a &quot;curse from Cthulhu-esque-thing from the other side&quot;, and then it could very well be 2. C. could either be 1 (Closed) or 3 (Open), if the Psychic either believes that &quot;all those so called &quot;Mages&quot; are just simply Psychics, the fools!&quot;, or it could be 3 Open, but in this case he would believe &quot;I'm a Psychic, but those other guys are actually doing &quot;Magic&quot;, whatever that is&quot;, in which case he believes his powers come from &quot;the power of the (his) mind&quot;, but that a Hermetic for example draws his powers from the &quot;Magic Mists&quot; or whatever; so this individual would actually believe in several different sources of power, rather than believing that &quot;everybody is a &quot;Mage&quot; &quot;. That's also an interesting view; an &quot;Awaken&quot; with an Open Paradigm can believe that some people are gifted by God, some are gifted by Spirits, others just do Science and yet others draw mystical energies from &quot;the primordial Mists&quot;, while he himself is an X-Men Professor Xavier type. I mean, Dr Strange and Professor Xavier would NEVER tell each other &quot;you know what, we just do the same thing all over, but I call it &quot;Magic&quot; while you call it &quot;psyonics&quot;, but it's actually all the same&quot;. In an Open Paradigm, that most likely DOESN'T HAPPEN. And finally for our Psychic, D. 2 (optional Foci), yes there are some funny songs he can chant to help him concentrate, but he just really needs to press his head and contract his sphincter really hard for his &quot;powers&quot; to work.<br /> <br /> That table also gives us a better vision as to what we want our Cosmology to be; I would get away with Avatars completely in here; maybe replace it for some other mechanics.<br /> <br /> And each one of these items can have interesting mechanics to it - for example, &quot;Divine Revelation&quot; requires strict adherence to certain precepts; that's a limitation, but on the other hand it allows you to do things that others cannot (like somebody said somewhere, you don't need to know about Blacksmithing to ask for your God(s) or the Spirits to give you a &quot;Sword to smite my enemies). A Materialistic/Mechanicist view would be less malleable, but have far more reliable and replicable results; a strict need for Foci would force you to always use something, but on the other hand, your effects are easier; and many many other ideas that I still haven't concocted (but that I expect that your minds can help me in expanding those ideas)<br /> <br /> What do you all think?<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T03:24:57-07:00","id":1533306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1531964-your-hypothetical-mage-30th-edition?p=1533297#post1533297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also not be against that other traditions/crafts could have their &quot;own things&quot;. Or maybe not just simply giving each small little group their own exclusive unicorn &quot;Discipline&quot; that them alone know, but rather a bag of &quot;Do-Like&quot; skills - for example, &quot;Sacred Geometry&quot; that could be a specialty of Hermetics and Choristers (Feng Shui for the Akashics), with special perks to it, and so forth and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The aforementioned <b>Prism of Focus</b> has a system in it where every Practice has a dot rating, representing how well you understand the inner workings of that Practice. (It also allows for \u201cSpecialized Practices\u201d, which are faction-specific variants of the general Practices that confer an additional benefit; so Do is a Specialized Practice of Martial Arts that's unique to the Akashayana.) The Abilities of Do and Hypertechnology get subsumed into this system, going from being separate Abilities in their own right to \u201cmerely\u201d being the Practices of Do and Hypertechnology.<br /> <br /> Something like that would be your \u201cDo-like skills\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  Streamlined 03-28-2024, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/